WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.602 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Even more important
than where it came from.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.738 align:start size:97% position:3%
The Chinese leadership
knew that they had a pretty

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.474 align:start size:97% position:3%
contagious, relatively
lethal virus on their hands

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:11.077
by the fall of '19,
and decided to put

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:13.580
tens of thousands of people
on airplanes and murder.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.116 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I say that
intentionally, murder

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:19.219 align:start position:0%
hundreds of thousands of
people all across this country.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.487
They had a choice to make.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.055
The choice they made
was load airplanes,

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.390
send them to Milan, Italy.

00:00:24.791 --> 00:00:27.027
The Chinese Communist Party
must be held accountable

00:00:27.027 --> 00:00:28.528
for this.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:30.463 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, they don't care
about human life, so be it.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:33.233
But when you transmit that
to the rest of the world

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:34.634
and you kill people
all around the world,

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:37.237
there's a place for
real accountability.

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:39.939
(dramatic music)

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I'm Dave Rubin,
and joining me today

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.747 align:start size:84% position:16%
is the former
director of the CIA,

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.517
a former secretary of state
and author of the new book,

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:54.054 align:start size:97% position:3%
"Never Give an Inch: Fighting
for the America I love,"

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:57.123 align:start size:97% position:3%
Secretary Mike Pompeo. Welcome
to, "The Rubin Report."

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.625 align:start size:81% position:19%
- Dave, it's great
to be with you.

00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.794
- I mentioned to you
right before we started

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:04.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I just did an hour
show blowing up the people

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.698
of the World Economic Forum,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:08.401
and now I get to talk
to an actual American,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.004 align:start size:84% position:16%
so I'm very relieved
at the moment.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:88% position:13%
That's how we're
starting this interview

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.841
with just relief on my part.

00:01:14.841 --> 00:01:16.476
I hope that's okay with you.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.912
- That is a great way
to begin an interview.

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:21.281
- And you did note that
you are not in Davos.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:22.982
Can I ask where you are?

00:01:22.982 --> 00:01:26.252
- Yeah, I'm in my home.
I'm in Virginia today.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.187
- Great. Great.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:28.888
All right. Well, there's a ton

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:30.123
to talk to you about obviously.

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.658
Before we get into
all of the CIA stuff

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:34.260
and secretary of state
stuff and Trump stuff

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.329
and Biden stuff,
and all that stuff,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.465
can you gimme like
a minute or two,

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:43.002
just kind Mike Pompeo 101
little bit of your history

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:46.005
that led you to doing
all of these things?

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.307
- Oh, goodness.

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:49.476
So, look, I grew up in
Santa Ana, California.

00:01:50.977 --> 00:01:55.048
My parents wanted to chart a
better life for their kids.

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:57.584 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have a older sister,
younger brother,

00:01:57.584 --> 00:01:59.586 align:start size:84% position:16%
much like many
parents in America.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.388 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then I got really lucky,
I got into West Point,

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.724
and so went to the United
States Military Academy,

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:07.927
served little over five
years on active duty.

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:09.195
I had a great assignment.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.697
Ronald Reagan was my
commander in chief.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was patrolling the East
German border in my M1 tank.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:16.669
There's not much better
for a 22-year-old kid

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:19.305
than rolling up and down
a Soviet communist border

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:20.240
in a M1 tank.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.608
It's all really good stuff.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:24.844
And then I went to law school,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.146
practiced law for
a couple of years,

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.580
and started a company in Kansas

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.517 align:start size:94% position:6%
with my three best friends
in the whole world,

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.852
married to a lovely
woman named Susan.

00:02:32.852 --> 00:02:35.722
We have one son, Nick,
who's now 32 years old

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:39.425 align:start size:97% position:3%
and married to a great
Christian lady named Rachel.

00:02:39.425 --> 00:02:41.427
And then I lost my mind after

00:02:41.427 --> 00:02:43.029
about eight or nine years
in the private sector,

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:46.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
ran for Congress, and
that led me to ultimately

00:02:46.733 --> 00:02:49.169 align:start size:88% position:13%
getting the opportunity
to serve America

00:02:49.169 --> 00:02:52.438 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the Trump administration
in those two roles.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
- All right. That's the
abbreviated bio let's say.

00:02:57.377 --> 00:03:01.181
Let me start this way for the
real portion of the interview.

00:03:01.181 --> 00:03:04.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
Right now when
people say CIA, FBI,

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:07.020
when people are hearing
all of what's going on

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.889
with the Twitter
files and seeming

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:13.126 align:start size:97% position:3%
government intelligence
agency collusion with big tech

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:88% position:13%
and all of these
things, there's a real,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:19.465 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think, warranted skepticism
about these agencies.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:21.801 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, can you just talk
to us a little bit about

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.604
what the agencies are like?

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.239
Is all of this stuff warranted,

00:03:26.239 --> 00:03:29.108 align:start size:84% position:16%
is some of our worries
unwarranted, et
cetera, et cetera?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.178
- No. The concern of
governmental power

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:35.081
is one of the reasons I
ran for Congress, right?

00:03:35.081 --> 00:03:38.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
Too much power in
Washington, D.C. unchecked

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:41.120
is something that America has
always had a responsibility

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:43.690
to protect against,
and you can see it.

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:47.393
I can speak most directly to
of the intelligence agencies,

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:48.595
the CIA.

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.063 align:start size:84% position:16%
I worked with the
FBI on some projects,

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.265 align:start size:81% position:19%
but I was never
responsible for it

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:55.235
in the same way that I got
a chance to peer inside CIA.

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:58.404 align:start size:84% position:16%
I took over from a man
named John Brennan,

00:03:58.404 --> 00:04:00.707
the previous director
who had politicized

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.976
that agency deeply.

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:05.545
He'd, I write about this
in, "Never Give an Inch."

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.714
He'd worked on this thing

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.849
that incorporated
the Steele dossier

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.352 align:start size:84% position:16%
that became the
Russia hoax in ways

00:04:12.352 --> 00:04:15.321 align:start size:97% position:3%
that were antithetical to good
analysis, good intelligence

00:04:15.321 --> 00:04:18.291 align:start size:97% position:3%
that is so important for the
United States of America.

00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:22.495
And I had to go back and
rebuild pieces of that.

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.197
But the good news was,

00:04:24.197 --> 00:04:25.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is different
from the State Department,

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.400
which is a big bureaucracy,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:32.038
which frankly we could talk
about is hugely problematic,

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.640
but different at the CIA.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.708
At the CIA, most of
the folks are people

00:04:36.843 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:81% position:19%
who want to do
America's mission,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.113
and so when I came in and
President Trump came in,

00:04:40.113 --> 00:04:42.682
yes, sir, got it. This is
the direction you're going.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.217
We're gonna go bang our
head against the wall.

00:04:44.217 --> 00:04:45.551
We're gonna go break through it,

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.453
and we're gonna deliver
for the American people

00:04:47.453 --> 00:04:49.522
as you have directed us to do.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:51.324
These are young men and
women who, you know,

00:04:51.324 --> 00:04:52.825
they just wanna put a
dagger in their mouth

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.662
and go out and collect
intelligence for us.

00:04:55.662 --> 00:04:58.264
And the risk is that you
have political leadership

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:00.133 align:start size:84% position:16%
and in the end
presidents own that.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
You have political
leadership that undermines

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:04.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
both America's confidence
in the institutions,

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:06.706
which is the skepticism
you're referring to.

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:11.678
But as equally bad as that,
as troubling as the absence

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:13.479
of confidence in
the institution is,

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.581
is they're not effective,
they're not on mission.

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:16.849
When they're spending their time

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.818
training on diversity,
equity, and inclusion,

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:23.823
when the green agenda and the
LGBTQ agenda come to dominate

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:27.994
the focus inside
these institutions,

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:32.398 align:start size:97% position:3%
you're undermining incredibly
powerful American tools

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.701
that have kept us all safe
for an awfully long time.

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.135
- So when you took the gig,

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:40.473
was it like day one that
you realized how politic

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
and the Obama staffing
and everything

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:45.311
that Brennan was doing, did
you realize it on day one,

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.413
how dirty the whole
thing had become

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:49.115
and how tough is it to go in

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.050
and try to clean up
some of that stuff?

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.619
- So I'd seen it
even before that,

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.455
I served on the House
Intelligence Committee,

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:59.592
so I had been watching the DNI
operation, the CIA operation,

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:03.229 align:start size:97% position:3%
all of the intelligence
folks for four or five years.

00:06:03.229 --> 00:06:05.164 align:start size:81% position:19%
And so I knew that
Brennan, look,

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:07.734
this is a director of the
CIA who refused to say

00:06:07.734 --> 00:06:11.571 align:start size:97% position:3%
that the agency spied on
foreigners, right? (chuckles)

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:12.839
- Right.

00:06:12.839 --> 00:06:16.209
- It's task is to go do
really good collections,

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.411
so presidents can
have good data sets

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:20.079
to make informed decisions.

00:06:20.079 --> 00:06:23.282
And so, I knew that Director
Brennan had taken this agency

00:06:23.282 --> 00:06:24.951
off mission, off its focus.

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:27.787
And so literally it's the
case, Dave, on day one,

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:31.858
I went in, built my team,
some of from the outside,

00:06:31.858 --> 00:06:34.894
most of it, frankly from the
inside, that were still great

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
and still are
great people there.

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:38.931
We identified leaders,
we identified people

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.633
who were pipehitters who
were willing to go crush it

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:43.903 align:start size:97% position:3%
on behalf of America and
change the focus of the agency

00:06:43.903 --> 00:06:45.605
to deliver for the president.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:48.441 align:start size:97% position:3%
- So, how has that now
changed since you are gone?

00:06:48.441 --> 00:06:50.710
And obviously we have
a new administration

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:52.612
and I suspect they probably like

00:06:52.612 --> 00:06:54.280 align:start size:84% position:16%
a lot of those
Brennan appointments

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:56.449
that were there, and ideas.

00:06:56.449 --> 00:06:59.485
- Yeah. Yeah. It's different.

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.154 align:start size:84% position:16%
I will say this, the
current director,

00:07:01.154 --> 00:07:03.689
Director Burns is
not John Brennan,

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:07.927
and so I think that's fantastic.

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:10.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
John, along with Director
Comey with the FBI,

00:07:10.863 --> 00:07:13.933 align:start size:84% position:16%
were a pair of truly
bad actors who,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.868
and I write about
this in the book,

00:07:15.868 --> 00:07:19.605 align:start size:88% position:13%
who on January 6th,
2017 when the president

00:07:19.605 --> 00:07:22.408
had not yet been sworn
in, went to Trump Tower,

00:07:22.408 --> 00:07:23.643
I was invited to be there.

00:07:23.643 --> 00:07:24.911
I was still just a
member of Congress,

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.846
I was the nominee to
be the CIA director,

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:29.081 align:start size:97% position:3%
went to Trump Tower,
basically told Donald Trump

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:31.651
that he was a Russian asset
or that they believed so,

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:33.820
and I am now even more convinced

00:07:33.820 --> 00:07:35.922
that they knew that wasn't true.

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:37.790
That they knew it was
based on unreliable,

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:40.326
unverified for sure information.

00:07:40.326 --> 00:07:44.497 align:start position:0%
And the harm that they did,
forget to me or to Donald Trump,

00:07:44.497 --> 00:07:46.966
the harm that they
did to our country

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:50.670 align:start size:97% position:3%
is just among the most
dangerous things I have seen

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.406 align:start size:97% position:3%
come out of the intelligence
community in my lifetime.

00:07:53.406 --> 00:07:55.308
- What do you make
of how nobody seems

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:57.009
to ever pay a price
for these things?

00:07:57.009 --> 00:07:59.111 align:start size:88% position:13%
So, when you talk about
the Steele dossier

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:02.415
coming out of this, or the 50
former intelligence officials

00:08:02.415 --> 00:08:04.784 align:start size:88% position:13%
that basically said
the Hunter Biden laptop

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:07.320 align:start size:97% position:3%
was Russian disinformation,
which we know obviously

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:08.654
it now was not.

00:08:08.654 --> 00:08:10.656 align:start position:0%
I think one of the
frustrations for average people

00:08:10.656 --> 00:08:12.225
is they see this and they go,

00:08:12.225 --> 00:08:14.360
Well, nobody seems
to ever get fired.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.763
Actually, the people who lie
end up with gigs on, "CNN"

00:08:17.763 --> 00:08:19.932
or in the government.

00:08:19.932 --> 00:08:22.468
- Yeah. One of my biggest
challenges was John Brennan

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:25.505 align:start size:97% position:3%
was out there on "MSNBC"
talking about all this stuff

00:08:25.505 --> 00:08:27.106
while I was trying
to run this CIA.

00:08:27.106 --> 00:08:29.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was hugely problematic
'cause you had

00:08:29.342 --> 00:08:32.245 align:start size:97% position:3%
some fraction of the workforce
that wanted to follow him.

00:08:32.245 --> 00:08:34.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
And more importantly,
you had this-

00:08:34.013 --> 00:08:35.882
- Are you guys not
told beforehand?

00:08:35.882 --> 00:08:37.783
I don't know who would
tell you, but I mean,

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.285
isn't shouldn't there
be some sort of code,

00:08:39.285 --> 00:08:40.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
like if you ran the thing,
you can't be on "MSNBC"

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:44.056
or "Fox" a week after you
leave to tell the secret.

00:08:44.056 --> 00:08:45.324
- Goodness. Yeah, yeah.

00:08:45.324 --> 00:08:47.093
And by the way, that
was common practice,

00:08:47.093 --> 00:08:48.661
a pretty common practice.

00:08:48.661 --> 00:08:50.296
Look, I don't have any problem

00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:51.697
if what you're going out there

00:08:51.697 --> 00:08:53.199 align:start size:97% position:3%
is to talk about the
greatness of the institution

00:08:53.199 --> 00:08:55.167 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you led and the people,
really the people, right?

00:08:55.167 --> 00:08:56.669 align:start size:84% position:16%
But when you're out
there telling stories,

00:08:56.669 --> 00:08:59.906
to your point about the
Russia hoax, John Brennan

00:08:59.906 --> 00:09:03.409
and the folks who signed
that document clearly knew

00:09:03.409 --> 00:09:05.878
that this was likely not
Russian disinformation,

00:09:05.878 --> 00:09:07.780
and so they caveat
it to be clever.

00:09:07.780 --> 00:09:10.650
But the truth is, I
think they all knew,

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.951
but they had a political agenda.

00:09:11.951 --> 00:09:13.653
And that's the danger.

00:09:15.688 --> 00:09:18.457
These institutions
matter an awful lot.

00:09:18.457 --> 00:09:21.861
We haven't spent as much
time talking about the FBI.

00:09:21.861 --> 00:09:22.795 align:start size:84% position:16%
But to your point
about accountability,

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.397
we know that McCabe lied.

00:09:24.397 --> 00:09:27.066 align:start size:97% position:3%
We know that the FBI
concluded that McCabe lied,

00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:29.969 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he's out on "CNN"
telling stories,

00:09:29.969 --> 00:09:32.672 align:start size:97% position:3%
pretending he was a good
actor inside that institution,

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:35.708 align:start size:97% position:3%
when in fact he, along
with the cohort around him,

00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:39.178
undermined the most basic
principles of our republic.

00:09:39.178 --> 00:09:41.747
- Who do you really put the
blame at with all of this?

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:44.383
Like, do you feel that
that's a Brennan to blame

00:09:44.383 --> 00:09:46.452
or was that purely
that he was doing

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:49.221
basically what Obama
appointed him to do?

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:53.693
- Dave, I always hold the
senior leaders accountable.

00:09:54.894 --> 00:09:56.395
And that holds true for
our administration too.

00:09:56.395 --> 00:09:58.397
The things we got wrong
were my responsibility

00:09:58.397 --> 00:09:59.532 align:start size:81% position:19%
or the president's
responsibility.

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:01.968
This isn't a partisan shot,

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:04.437
so I hold President
Obama responsible.

00:10:04.437 --> 00:10:06.505 align:start size:84% position:16%
In fact, with respect
to this dossier

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:09.008 align:start size:88% position:13%
and the intelligence
report that was written,

00:10:09.008 --> 00:10:11.110 align:start size:84% position:16%
Obama had directed
that report be written

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:15.247
and publicized in the fall
of what would've been 2016

00:10:17.049 --> 00:10:18.651
after the election.

00:10:18.651 --> 00:10:20.987 align:start size:84% position:16%
He directed that they
write this report

00:10:20.987 --> 00:10:22.521
and that they make
a classified version

00:10:22.521 --> 00:10:24.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
and an unclassified
version that was released.

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:26.959 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's unheard of
to have that happen,

00:10:26.959 --> 00:10:29.895
and so this was directed
from the highest levels.

00:10:29.895 --> 00:10:31.831
Last thought, people matter.

00:10:31.831 --> 00:10:36.068
And so every president has
to be incredibly focused

00:10:36.068 --> 00:10:40.139 align:start size:97% position:3%
from before day one on
bringing the right people in

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:43.409 align:start position:0%
that not only share their policy
views, but their value set.

00:10:43.409 --> 00:10:46.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I think you can see
one of the things I regret

00:10:46.679 --> 00:10:49.548 align:start size:97% position:3%
is that Director Comey
wasn't replaced immediately

00:10:49.548 --> 00:10:51.617
at the beginning of
our administration.

00:10:51.617 --> 00:10:54.387 align:start size:88% position:13%
He sat inside of our
team while he was trying

00:10:54.387 --> 00:10:57.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
to undermine everything
it was that we were doing.

00:10:57.123 --> 00:11:00.059
- So, do you blame your
former boss for that?

00:11:00.059 --> 00:11:01.460
Like do you think
he was just not,

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:03.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
didn't realize the
magnitude of the problem?

00:11:03.663 --> 00:11:06.032 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because that is one of the
things people say, Hey, Obama,

00:11:06.032 --> 00:11:07.433
you may not like what he did,

00:11:07.433 --> 00:11:09.568 align:start size:97% position:3%
but he did staff these
places the way that he wanted

00:11:09.568 --> 00:11:12.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
while Trump didn't realize
how many layers down,

00:11:12.605 --> 00:11:15.508
something to that effect,
that that's one of the kind

00:11:15.508 --> 00:11:17.109 align:start size:81% position:19%
of memes out there
on this thing.

00:11:17.109 --> 00:11:18.577 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah. I even think President
Trump himself has said

00:11:18.577 --> 00:11:20.613 align:start size:84% position:16%
that he came in
new without knowing

00:11:20.613 --> 00:11:21.747
a whole lot of folks in town,

00:11:21.747 --> 00:11:24.250 align:start size:84% position:16%
which was a positive,
a good thing.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:26.118
I'm in support of that.

00:11:26.118 --> 00:11:28.287 align:start size:84% position:16%
But also had the
downside of the fact

00:11:29.588 --> 00:11:31.023 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he had some
missteps at the front end

00:11:31.023 --> 00:11:32.725
in terms of people.

00:11:32.725 --> 00:11:34.827
The second thing is,
is we didn't get our
team on the field.

00:11:34.827 --> 00:11:36.696 align:start size:84% position:16%
So not only were
there some selections

00:11:36.696 --> 00:11:38.197
that weren't the right ones,

00:11:38.197 --> 00:11:39.932
we spent an awful lot of
time waiting for our folks

00:11:39.932 --> 00:11:42.568
to get the clearances complete,

00:11:42.568 --> 00:11:45.037
get the Senate to confirm
them, get them in position.

00:11:45.037 --> 00:11:49.108
We lived the first year and a
half or two of our entire time

00:11:49.108 --> 00:11:51.944
of half of our time
working with folks

00:11:51.944 --> 00:11:54.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
who'd been appointed by
president other than the one

00:11:54.146 --> 00:11:58.150
that the people had elected in
November of 2016. That's bad.

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
Whoever the next
conservative president is,

00:12:00.319 --> 00:12:01.554
they've got to get that right.

00:12:01.554 --> 00:12:03.756
They gotta show up
day one, helmet on,

00:12:03.756 --> 00:12:06.525
ready to thrive these
people into the team,

00:12:06.525 --> 00:12:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that we have our team,
we have our leaders,

00:12:09.195 --> 00:12:12.498
they are out executing with a
viciousness that is required

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:15.034 align:start size:88% position:13%
to push back against the
administrative state.

00:12:15.034 --> 00:12:16.569
- So speaking of that
administrative state,

00:12:16.569 --> 00:12:19.205
I'm sure you've seen some
of the Twitter file leaks

00:12:19.205 --> 00:12:21.941
and the emails that went
from intelligence agencies

00:12:21.941 --> 00:12:24.410
to the employees at Twitter.

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:26.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, were they
overstepping their bounds

00:12:26.879 --> 00:12:31.117 align:start position:0%
and at what point is that a
violation of our first amendment

00:12:31.117 --> 00:12:33.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
if the government is in
essence coercing a company

00:12:33.619 --> 00:12:35.354
to silence people?

00:12:35.354 --> 00:12:37.623
- Yeah, you can either
have command and control

00:12:37.623 --> 00:12:39.925 align:start size:88% position:13%
or you can have coercion
in this case, right?

00:12:39.925 --> 00:12:42.027
And the net effect is identical.

00:12:42.027 --> 00:12:45.397 align:start size:97% position:3%
I think you can pretty
clearly see this was coercion,

00:12:45.397 --> 00:12:47.133
so lawyers can all tell us

00:12:47.133 --> 00:12:48.901 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether that invokes
the first right

00:12:48.901 --> 00:12:50.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
or if you have
government action or not.

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:52.772
I don't really, well,
here's what we know.

00:12:52.772 --> 00:12:55.341
We know with absolute certainty

00:12:55.341 --> 00:12:58.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the political
actors in the White House

00:12:58.944 --> 00:13:01.046 align:start size:84% position:16%
were giving guidance
to these folks

00:13:01.046 --> 00:13:02.748
to censor conservative ideas.

00:13:02.748 --> 00:13:06.886
Not viewpoint neutral, this is
not about keeping the Taliban

00:13:06.886 --> 00:13:09.121
or ISIS off of Twitter.

00:13:09.121 --> 00:13:11.857
This is about political actors

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:15.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
seeking to manipulate
speech in America in a way

00:13:15.661 --> 00:13:18.931
that promoted a governmental
viewpoint, that is dangerous.

00:13:18.931 --> 00:13:21.267
I'm happy to see that the
American people can see it,

00:13:21.267 --> 00:13:23.702
because in the end,
Dave, you know this,

00:13:23.702 --> 00:13:25.905
most of the recourse, to your
point about accountability,

00:13:25.905 --> 00:13:29.408 align:start size:88% position:13%
most of the recourse
comes through political
accountability.

00:13:29.408 --> 00:13:32.244 align:start size:97% position:3%
Justice departments are
responsive to the presidents

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:34.580
that put them together,

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:36.649 align:start size:88% position:13%
while they have a
element of independence.

00:13:36.649 --> 00:13:37.850
Make no mistake about it.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:39.118
The attorney general
works for the president

00:13:39.118 --> 00:13:40.386
of the United States of America,

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:42.054
and we can see that
plain as day-to-day

00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:43.489
in the way Merrick Garland

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:45.024
is delivering this
justice department

00:13:45.024 --> 00:13:47.493
and weaponizing so much of
what they're doing there.

00:13:47.493 --> 00:13:49.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
- So, let's talk
about that actually.

00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:50.896
'Cause obviously the
big thing at the moment

00:13:50.896 --> 00:13:53.032
are these classified documents.

00:13:53.032 --> 00:13:56.435
We went through six months ago
what Trump had at Mar-a-Lago,

00:13:56.435 --> 00:13:58.838 align:start size:97% position:3%
and the president is allowed
to declassify things.

00:13:58.838 --> 00:14:01.707
But the media was telling you
the walls are closing in again

00:14:01.707 --> 00:14:04.210
and okay, it doesn't seem
as if much has happened.

00:14:04.210 --> 00:14:05.444
But now Biden's in the midst

00:14:05.444 --> 00:14:07.546
of one of these
scandals himself.

00:14:07.546 --> 00:14:10.749 align:start size:97% position:3%
What should the policy,
what actually is the policy

00:14:10.749 --> 00:14:12.351
on this sort of thing?

00:14:12.351 --> 00:14:13.619
Like, one of the things

00:14:13.619 --> 00:14:14.887
that I've heard Biden
say a couple times is,

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:16.689
well, it was a small
amount of documents

00:14:16.689 --> 00:14:18.891
as if that somehow makes
it a little bit better.

00:14:18.891 --> 00:14:20.226
I'm pretty sure you don't want

00:14:20.226 --> 00:14:21.594
any classified docs out, right?

00:14:21.594 --> 00:14:23.329
Is that fair to say?

00:14:23.329 --> 00:14:24.997
- It seems right, Dave.

00:14:24.997 --> 00:14:26.532 align:start size:84% position:16%
If it's classified,
it has a place

00:14:26.532 --> 00:14:29.368
and that place isn't next to
your Corvette in the garage.

00:14:29.368 --> 00:14:31.971
By the way, it's also
not at Mar-a-Lago.

00:14:31.971 --> 00:14:34.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
And by the way, it
wasn't on your Blackberry

00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:35.941
when you were Hillary Clinton.

00:14:35.941 --> 00:14:37.209
The first time I
dealt with this,

00:14:37.209 --> 00:14:38.477
when I sat on the
Benghazi committee

00:14:38.477 --> 00:14:40.779
with Jim Jordan and Trey Gowdy,

00:14:40.779 --> 00:14:43.449
when you had senior
American officials

00:14:43.449 --> 00:14:44.917 align:start size:84% position:16%
exchanging classified
information

00:14:44.917 --> 00:14:48.087 align:start position:0%
across an unsecured Blackberry,
and you had all this stuff

00:14:48.087 --> 00:14:50.356
in the server up at Hillary
Clinton's place in New York.

00:14:50.356 --> 00:14:53.292
I lived this where we
were trying to unpack

00:14:53.292 --> 00:14:56.362 align:start position:0%
exactly the risk she had created
to America by doing this.

00:14:56.362 --> 00:14:58.697
My theory on this one,
again, not partisan,

00:14:58.697 --> 00:15:00.566 align:start size:88% position:13%
classified information,
protect it.

00:15:00.566 --> 00:15:01.667
If it shouldn't be classified,

00:15:01.667 --> 00:15:03.269
if it's overclassified, fine.

00:15:03.269 --> 00:15:04.837
Declassify it, get it out,

00:15:04.837 --> 00:15:07.439 align:start size:97% position:3%
release it to, "The
Washington Post," sign me up.

00:15:07.439 --> 00:15:10.309 align:start size:88% position:13%
But if the decision
was that this is needed

00:15:10.309 --> 00:15:12.611 align:start size:97% position:3%
to protect an American
secret or American soldiers

00:15:12.611 --> 00:15:15.281 align:start position:0%
or sailors or airmen or
marines somewhere in the world,

00:15:15.281 --> 00:15:17.483
then for goodness sakes,
no one, not a president,

00:15:17.483 --> 00:15:19.985
not not a CIA director
or secretary of state,

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:22.988 align:start size:94% position:6%
no one should be absolved
from responsibility

00:15:22.988 --> 00:15:24.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
for managing that
information appropriately,

00:15:24.823 --> 00:15:28.460
and so I hope this
will be managed in a
way that is neutral.

00:15:28.460 --> 00:15:31.830
And I'd say one last thing,
Dave, neutral in two ways.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.199
One, it shouldn't be
political, Rs, Ds,

00:15:34.199 --> 00:15:36.802 align:start size:88% position:13%
conservatives, liberals,
but neutral also,

00:15:36.802 --> 00:15:38.671
and I write about
this in the book.

00:15:38.671 --> 00:15:40.105
We didn't prosecute,

00:15:40.105 --> 00:15:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
we didn't get any anything
to Hillary Clinton.

00:15:41.674 --> 00:15:44.610
There were lots of young
soldiers, young Marines,

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:45.778
who had made mistakes

00:15:45.778 --> 00:15:47.313 align:start size:88% position:13%
in how they handle
classified information.

00:15:47.313 --> 00:15:50.015
They were punished, and
so we should make sure

00:15:50.015 --> 00:15:51.684
that you don't get off scot free

00:15:51.684 --> 00:15:54.320
just because you have
power and influence,

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:57.323 align:start position:0%
and you are punished if you
are someone who is more junior,

00:15:57.323 --> 00:16:00.359
whether you're a GS12 at
the Department of Energy

00:16:00.359 --> 00:16:03.996 align:start size:81% position:19%
or a young private
in the Marines.

00:16:03.996 --> 00:16:05.798 align:start size:84% position:16%
We should make sure
that in America

00:16:05.798 --> 00:16:07.800
the law is applied evenly,

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:10.436
both left and right
and up and down.

00:16:10.436 --> 00:16:11.737
- That would be refreshing.

00:16:11.737 --> 00:16:12.671
I don't even know
if you're allowed

00:16:12.671 --> 00:16:13.872
to answer this next question,

00:16:13.872 --> 00:16:16.642 align:start size:84% position:16%
but how do you guys
actually decide

00:16:16.642 --> 00:16:19.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
what really is that
highest level classified?

00:16:19.211 --> 00:16:22.481
Is there a standard
policy on everything

00:16:22.481 --> 00:16:24.450
or do they bring
things to your desk

00:16:24.450 --> 00:16:26.485 align:start size:88% position:13%
and you have people
making arguments for you

00:16:26.485 --> 00:16:28.787
that you have to make
that final call on.

00:16:28.787 --> 00:16:30.189
- Some of each.

00:16:30.189 --> 00:16:32.825 align:start position:0%
So there's a process, a
detailed classification process

00:16:32.825 --> 00:16:35.027
within the United
States government.

00:16:35.027 --> 00:16:37.029 align:start size:84% position:16%
The Department of
Defense has a process,

00:16:37.029 --> 00:16:39.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
the intelligence agencies
each have a process.

00:16:39.131 --> 00:16:41.400
They roughly mirror each other,

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:44.203
but decision makers at every
level are making decisions

00:16:44.203 --> 00:16:45.771
about how to classify.

00:16:45.771 --> 00:16:47.773
There are categories of things.

00:16:47.773 --> 00:16:50.009 align:start size:88% position:13%
If there are things
about operative
somewhere in the world,

00:16:50.009 --> 00:16:53.312
it gets a certain classified,
so there is a rubric designed

00:16:53.312 --> 00:16:56.181 align:start size:97% position:3%
to try and get these
classification levels right.

00:16:56.181 --> 00:16:57.416
Look at the edge.

00:16:57.416 --> 00:16:58.817
I'm sure there's people
making judgment calls,

00:16:58.817 --> 00:17:00.219
maybe some of them political.

00:17:00.219 --> 00:17:02.554
I didn't see much of
that inside the CIA,

00:17:02.554 --> 00:17:04.523 align:start size:88% position:13%
mostly I saw people
trying to get it right.

00:17:04.523 --> 00:17:07.059
And then there were
many, many occasions

00:17:07.059 --> 00:17:08.694
when things were brought to me,

00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:11.663
and for whatever reason I
wanted them declassified.

00:17:11.663 --> 00:17:13.699 align:start size:97% position:3%
I felt it was important that
the American people knew.

00:17:13.699 --> 00:17:15.234
I thought that the risk,

00:17:15.234 --> 00:17:17.202
whatever that might have been
two years ago, five years ago,

00:17:17.202 --> 00:17:18.437
was diminished.

00:17:18.437 --> 00:17:20.472
And so I would send
it back down and say,

00:17:20.472 --> 00:17:21.640
we needed to declassify this.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:23.175 align:start size:88% position:13%
A little bit of
process, but in the end,

00:17:23.175 --> 00:17:26.478 align:start size:97% position:3%
between the senior
leadership and the president,

00:17:26.478 --> 00:17:29.415
we could always get it to the
right level of classification.

00:17:29.415 --> 00:17:30.883 align:start size:97% position:3%
There are a handful of
times I went the other way.

00:17:30.883 --> 00:17:32.718 align:start size:97% position:3%
I saw something like,
"What the heck's that doing

00:17:32.718 --> 00:17:34.586
out at in the free space.

00:17:34.586 --> 00:17:37.022
We need to try to make sure
we secure that information

00:17:37.022 --> 00:17:39.058
at least for a little while."

00:17:39.058 --> 00:17:41.427
- Are you worried at all
that as people kind of see

00:17:41.427 --> 00:17:44.430
how dysfunctional Washington is,

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:46.665
or just how crazy the
machine seems to be

00:17:46.665 --> 00:17:48.267 align:start size:84% position:16%
as we've, you know,
because of technology,

00:17:48.267 --> 00:17:50.335 align:start size:84% position:16%
we can look under
the hood now in a way

00:17:50.335 --> 00:17:52.704 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you couldn't,
say 40 years ago that,

00:17:52.704 --> 00:17:54.873
that we're not gonna
get the quality person

00:17:54.873 --> 00:17:56.875 align:start size:84% position:16%
that you want working
in these agencies

00:17:56.875 --> 00:17:58.143 align:start size:81% position:19%
because people are
just gonna say,

00:17:58.143 --> 00:17:59.711
no, I'd rather be in
the private sector.

00:17:59.711 --> 00:18:02.347
I just see this thing
as a big freaking mess.

00:18:02.347 --> 00:18:04.016 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, I understand
you're saying

00:18:04.016 --> 00:18:05.284
there's obviously a lot
of great people there,

00:18:05.284 --> 00:18:07.286
but that over time
that there will be

00:18:07.286 --> 00:18:10.022
a sort of a draining of that.

00:18:11.156 --> 00:18:12.691 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yes. I'm worried about
it in two respects.

00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:15.427 align:start size:84% position:16%
One, in the true sense
that you described,

00:18:15.427 --> 00:18:18.030
good people will decide
not worth the candle.

00:18:18.030 --> 00:18:20.566 align:start size:88% position:13%
Yeah. For financial
reasons, family reasons,

00:18:20.566 --> 00:18:22.901
who needs the headache
reasons, all the above.

00:18:22.901 --> 00:18:24.703
The second reason
I worry about this,

00:18:24.703 --> 00:18:26.271
and I write about this,

00:18:26.271 --> 00:18:28.774
and this is why you
can't give an inch,

00:18:28.774 --> 00:18:30.709 align:start size:88% position:13%
that's why I titled
the book the way I did.

00:18:30.709 --> 00:18:32.845 align:start size:97% position:3%
The bias will be that
people of the left will say,

00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:34.313
yeah, I wanna be
part of government.

00:18:34.313 --> 00:18:38.117
And conservative will say, I
want to go live my life, right?

00:18:39.251 --> 00:18:41.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that bias, I
think already exists

00:18:41.920 --> 00:18:43.689
inside these bureaucracies.

00:18:43.689 --> 00:18:47.025
I come from a place where
government is something

00:18:47.025 --> 00:18:49.795
that you look at and you go,
Yeah, I'm a little skeptical.

00:18:49.795 --> 00:18:52.064
And the private sector
should be flourishing

00:18:52.064 --> 00:18:54.233 align:start size:88% position:13%
and delivering in
churches and synagogues,

00:18:54.233 --> 00:18:55.601
and boy scout troops.

00:18:55.601 --> 00:18:57.035
That's the place
America was made.

00:18:57.035 --> 00:18:59.238 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so conservatives
tend to say,

00:18:59.238 --> 00:19:00.672
I'm good. I'm living here.

00:19:00.672 --> 00:19:02.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm living my
great life in Texas

00:19:02.241 --> 00:19:05.277 align:start position:0%
or my wonderful life in Southern
Illinois, wherever you are.

00:19:05.277 --> 00:19:07.746
And say, you know, why'd
I go to Washington for,

00:19:07.746 --> 00:19:10.449 align:start size:84% position:16%
and liberals are
dying for that power.

00:19:10.449 --> 00:19:14.353 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, not only do you have
a net decrease in talent

00:19:14.353 --> 00:19:16.555 align:start size:81% position:19%
that I worry about
and excellence,

00:19:16.555 --> 00:19:17.789
but you'll get a bias.

00:19:17.789 --> 00:19:21.260
The best people who are
conservative thinkers,

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:23.061
people who are good
operators will say,

00:19:23.061 --> 00:19:25.764
nah, I'm not gonna go do that.

00:19:25.764 --> 00:19:27.299
- What do you do about that?

00:19:27.299 --> 00:19:29.034
I mean, that one seems
almost unwinnable to me

00:19:29.034 --> 00:19:31.470
because that's just
the nature of power

00:19:31.470 --> 00:19:32.905
versus the individual.

00:19:32.905 --> 00:19:34.473 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you're just
gonna self-select out

00:19:34.473 --> 00:19:35.974
because you want
to go do something

00:19:35.974 --> 00:19:38.377
in a functional free atmosphere.

00:19:38.377 --> 00:19:40.579 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that's not really
the government.

00:19:40.579 --> 00:19:42.281 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, is there any
solution to that?

00:19:42.281 --> 00:19:44.716
- Yes, I'm gonna provide
the solution right now.

00:19:44.716 --> 00:19:46.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Wow.
- To your entire audience.

00:19:46.084 --> 00:19:47.319
- All right.

00:19:47.319 --> 00:19:50.189
- Go spend some part
of your life serving.

00:19:50.189 --> 00:19:51.590
Doesn't have to be
in Washington, D.C.,

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:53.559
it doesn't even have
to be in government.

00:19:53.559 --> 00:19:55.360
But different people will be

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:57.029 align:start size:81% position:19%
in different parts
of their life.

00:19:57.029 --> 00:19:59.531
Take a couple years, four
years, two, whatever it is,

00:19:59.531 --> 00:20:00.732
and go serve.

00:20:00.732 --> 00:20:02.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can do it as a
deacon at your church.

00:20:02.701 --> 00:20:04.436 align:start size:81% position:19%
You can do that
coaching someone's

00:20:04.436 --> 00:20:06.538
little league baseball team.

00:20:06.538 --> 00:20:07.940
You can do it in
Washington, D.C.,

00:20:07.940 --> 00:20:10.209 align:start size:97% position:3%
you can run for city council,
or even better still,

00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:12.344
run for school board
and go fix the crap

00:20:12.344 --> 00:20:14.746
that's being taught
in our schools today.

00:20:14.746 --> 00:20:16.148 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so, I'm not
only gonna tell you

00:20:16.148 --> 00:20:17.916
that there's a solution to this.

00:20:17.916 --> 00:20:19.518
I'm gonna be part
of the solution

00:20:19.518 --> 00:20:22.821
by urging people who
share our value system,

00:20:22.821 --> 00:20:25.824 align:start size:84% position:16%
who understand the
Judeo-Christian
heritage of America

00:20:25.824 --> 00:20:29.595
in the most fundamental way
and say, all right, I get it.

00:20:29.595 --> 00:20:32.130
It's really wonderful to be
out here living my own life.

00:20:32.130 --> 00:20:35.200 align:start size:97% position:3%
But at some point in your
20s, in your 30s, in your 50s,

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:37.436
whatever, go spend a
little bit of time.

00:20:37.436 --> 00:20:39.838
This is the greatest nation of
the history of civilization.

00:20:39.838 --> 00:20:41.940 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we each can find
a way and a place

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:43.775
to give back just a little bit.

00:20:43.775 --> 00:20:46.645
- So, let's shift a little
bit to the second portion

00:20:46.645 --> 00:20:48.513
of your job in the
Trump administration.

00:20:48.513 --> 00:20:50.382
So you had about a, it
was about a year plus,

00:20:50.382 --> 00:20:51.984
right, as CIA director,

00:20:51.984 --> 00:20:53.785 align:start size:84% position:16%
and then you had the
last couple years

00:20:53.785 --> 00:20:56.355
as the secretary of state.

00:20:56.355 --> 00:20:58.357
Did you expect that
kind of transition?

00:20:58.357 --> 00:20:59.791
Did the phone just ring one day?

00:20:59.791 --> 00:21:02.060
Were you looking for a new gig?

00:21:02.060 --> 00:21:03.362 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, a little
different than that.

00:21:03.362 --> 00:21:06.665
I got a quick heads
up that the president

00:21:06.665 --> 00:21:08.467
was thinking about
making a change.

00:21:08.467 --> 00:21:09.968 align:start size:81% position:19%
It was apparent
to the whole world

00:21:09.968 --> 00:21:11.803 align:start size:97% position:3%
that he wasn't pleased with
the current secretary of state

00:21:11.803 --> 00:21:14.339
or then Secretary of
State Rex Tillerson,

00:21:14.339 --> 00:21:16.074
so that didn't come
as a surprise to me.

00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:17.376 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I got a little
bit of heads up

00:21:17.376 --> 00:21:20.078
from then Chief of Staff Kelly.

00:21:20.078 --> 00:21:22.080 align:start size:97% position:3%
And then one day the president
asked me to stay behind

00:21:22.080 --> 00:21:23.415 align:start size:84% position:16%
after I had briefed
him and said,

00:21:23.415 --> 00:21:24.983 align:start size:88% position:13%
Hey, I'm thinking about
making this change.

00:21:24.983 --> 00:21:26.518
I'm thinking about maybe you.

00:21:27.519 --> 00:21:29.154
I loved what I was doing, Dave,

00:21:29.154 --> 00:21:32.124 align:start size:88% position:13%
and I had a lot of work
to do still at CIA,

00:21:32.124 --> 00:21:33.759 align:start size:81% position:19%
and so it was very
mixed feelings.

00:21:33.759 --> 00:21:35.460 align:start size:97% position:3%
But in the end, when the
president asked you to serve,

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:36.295
you do it.

00:21:37.396 --> 00:21:38.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
It was a couple
weeks later, I think,

00:21:38.964 --> 00:21:41.333
he called me and said, Hey,
I want you to come do this.

00:21:41.333 --> 00:21:43.735 align:start size:97% position:3%
I of course immediately
said, yes, sir, here we go,

00:21:43.735 --> 00:21:45.404
helmet on, let's get after it.

00:21:45.404 --> 00:21:46.972
- And what kind
of shift is that?

00:21:46.972 --> 00:21:50.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause obviously these are
extremely different positions.

00:21:50.542 --> 00:21:52.144
- Big shift.

00:21:52.144 --> 00:21:54.046
You had the glory at the CIA

00:21:54.046 --> 00:21:56.415
of never having to
deal with the media

00:21:56.415 --> 00:21:58.050
and immediately moved
to the State Department

00:21:58.050 --> 00:21:59.318
where they are front and center

00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:01.253
and they sit in the
back of your airplane

00:22:01.253 --> 00:22:02.454
when you travel
around the world.

00:22:02.454 --> 00:22:04.890
And you had a team
that was much bigger,

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:06.591
70,000 or so people

00:22:06.591 --> 00:22:08.694
at the United States
Department of State.

00:22:08.694 --> 00:22:11.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
And you also had a bureaucracy
that had three unions,

00:22:11.863 --> 00:22:13.498 align:start size:84% position:16%
a set of civil service
rules that mean

00:22:13.498 --> 00:22:15.767 align:start size:84% position:16%
you essentially
can't fire anybody.

00:22:15.767 --> 00:22:18.303 align:start size:84% position:16%
A fundamentally
different institution

00:22:18.303 --> 00:22:20.238
that also had good people.

00:22:20.238 --> 00:22:21.273
But who...

00:22:24.309 --> 00:22:25.510 align:start size:84% position:16%
It is a left of
center organization,

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:26.712
but even more troubling,

00:22:26.712 --> 00:22:29.181 align:start size:84% position:16%
it is an establishment
organization.

00:22:29.181 --> 00:22:32.351
And so whether Republican or
Democrat, that institution,

00:22:32.351 --> 00:22:35.454
the inertia inside of
the Department of State

00:22:35.454 --> 00:22:39.591
was something that we all just
struggled to light a fire on,

00:22:39.591 --> 00:22:42.728 align:start position:0%
get after them, make them
effective, make them efficient,

00:22:42.728 --> 00:22:45.497 align:start size:84% position:16%
and turn their
focus on delivering,

00:22:45.497 --> 00:22:47.232 align:start size:88% position:13%
putting American
people first in the way

00:22:47.232 --> 00:22:49.301 align:start size:88% position:13%
that President Trump and
I were thinking about

00:22:49.301 --> 00:22:50.736
our place in the world.

00:22:50.736 --> 00:22:52.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
- But you got stuff done.
- We did.

00:22:53.905 --> 00:22:55.440 align:start position:0%
- I mean, we got a couple
peace deals in the Middle East,

00:22:55.440 --> 00:22:57.476
which I thought everybody
was for, my whole life.

00:22:57.476 --> 00:22:58.877
everyone was for
that sort of thing.

00:22:58.877 --> 00:23:02.013
Suddenly when Trump does
it, it's no good, right?

00:23:02.013 --> 00:23:05.884
- It turns out that we
didn't get the plaudits

00:23:05.884 --> 00:23:07.753
that it's so deserved.

00:23:07.753 --> 00:23:10.188
But in the end it isn't
about getting kudos,

00:23:10.188 --> 00:23:12.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the end it's about
delivering good outcomes.

00:23:12.891 --> 00:23:15.394
These Abraham Accords and I
spent a fair amount of time

00:23:15.394 --> 00:23:17.896
talking about it, wasn't
just me, Jared Kushner,

00:23:17.896 --> 00:23:19.898
Steven Mnuchin, we had
two great ambassadors,

00:23:19.898 --> 00:23:23.902
David Friedman and John
Rakolta in the Emirates.

00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:26.538
We had a great team just
working this problem set.

00:23:26.538 --> 00:23:28.807
The Lord blessed us with
Prime Minister Netanyahu,

00:23:28.807 --> 00:23:31.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
Donald Trump, Mohammed
bin Salman in the Kingdom,

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.345 align:start size:84% position:16%
MBZ in the Emirates,
great leaders,

00:23:33.345 --> 00:23:35.280
who are prepared
to take some risks.

00:23:36.448 --> 00:23:38.150
And the great news
is we got peace.

00:23:38.150 --> 00:23:40.218 align:start size:88% position:13%
These nations now aren't
trying to wipe Israel

00:23:40.218 --> 00:23:41.319
off the face of the earth.

00:23:41.319 --> 00:23:43.054 align:start size:84% position:16%
That is a wonderfully
good thing.

00:23:43.054 --> 00:23:45.357
But importantly for
the American people,

00:23:45.357 --> 00:23:47.826
the chance that we
have to send our kids

00:23:47.826 --> 00:23:50.595
to fight and die in the
Middle East now is lower.

00:23:50.595 --> 00:23:53.465 align:start size:97% position:3%
There's more stability,
more prosperity, more peace.

00:23:53.465 --> 00:23:55.000
And as I always
thought about it,

00:23:55.000 --> 00:23:57.169
that was the best outcome
of the Abraham Accords.

00:23:57.169 --> 00:24:00.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
The fact that we now have
friends and partners.

00:24:00.272 --> 00:24:04.009
We had isolated Iran and
it was much less likely

00:24:04.009 --> 00:24:06.611 align:start size:97% position:3%
that some president someday
is going to announce

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:09.281
that we're deploying
Marines and soldiers

00:24:09.281 --> 00:24:11.783
and Air Force guys and
gals to the Middle East

00:24:11.783 --> 00:24:13.285
to fight some Middle East War.

00:24:13.285 --> 00:24:16.154
America doesn't need that. The
Middle East doesn't need it.

00:24:16.154 --> 00:24:18.089
And that's why I'm just so happy

00:24:18.089 --> 00:24:19.591
that we were able
to get that done.

00:24:19.591 --> 00:24:21.893
- It's so weird because
even though it was only

00:24:21.893 --> 00:24:23.829 align:start size:84% position:16%
basically three
years ago, it's like,

00:24:23.829 --> 00:24:25.797 align:start size:84% position:16%
it feels like a
real distant memory

00:24:25.797 --> 00:24:27.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
that this
administration, you know,

00:24:27.532 --> 00:24:29.901 align:start size:97% position:3%
at first they were saying
don't even say Abraham Accords

00:24:29.901 --> 00:24:31.503
and they really didn't
wanna give any credit.

00:24:31.503 --> 00:24:34.706 align:start size:97% position:3%
How tenuous was it as you
guys were making these deals?

00:24:34.706 --> 00:24:36.775
Like, did you feel
like at any moment

00:24:36.775 --> 00:24:37.909 align:start size:81% position:19%
the whole thing
could fall through

00:24:37.909 --> 00:24:39.544
or there was gonna be a leak

00:24:39.544 --> 00:24:42.347 align:start size:84% position:16%
that was gonna ruin
it for another country
or whatever else?

00:24:43.448 --> 00:24:45.617 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, Dave, we
suffered lots of leaks

00:24:45.617 --> 00:24:49.588 align:start size:97% position:3%
and leaks on this particular
effort were very real

00:24:49.588 --> 00:24:52.257
and put a lot at risk because
you had Middle East leaders

00:24:52.257 --> 00:24:53.859 align:start size:88% position:13%
taking real risks
inside their countries.

00:24:53.859 --> 00:24:56.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
The historic argument that
the street will rise up

00:24:56.928 --> 00:24:58.630 align:start size:84% position:16%
and they'll be rioting
and bad things,

00:24:58.630 --> 00:25:00.098
and they'll overthrow regimes

00:25:00.098 --> 00:25:04.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the Palestinians will
start creating chaos,

00:25:04.603 --> 00:25:06.404
they'll be World War
III was very real.

00:25:06.404 --> 00:25:10.041
That didn't change, that
perception didn't change.

00:25:10.041 --> 00:25:11.510 align:start size:84% position:16%
So yeah, it was
tenuous till the end.

00:25:11.510 --> 00:25:13.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
None of these deals are
ever over till they're over.

00:25:13.879 --> 00:25:15.413
And we had to get a
lot of moving parts

00:25:15.413 --> 00:25:17.415 align:start size:97% position:3%
headed in the right
direction at the same time,

00:25:17.415 --> 00:25:19.184
and so there was complexity.

00:25:20.585 --> 00:25:23.955 align:start size:97% position:3%
And it took us two and a half
years to actually deliver

00:25:23.955 --> 00:25:26.892
from conceptual
idea to execution

00:25:26.892 --> 00:25:30.161 align:start size:97% position:3%
on the south lawn of the
White House, a glorious day.

00:25:30.161 --> 00:25:31.429
Good stuff for those countries

00:25:31.429 --> 00:25:32.764
and important for
our country too.

00:25:32.764 --> 00:25:34.566 align:start size:88% position:13%
- What kind of pushback
did you guys get

00:25:34.566 --> 00:25:37.102 align:start size:88% position:13%
from that sort of
state that you describe

00:25:37.102 --> 00:25:38.670
of these people that
don't change much?

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:41.273 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I had Netanyahu on
about a month and a half ago,

00:25:41.273 --> 00:25:42.807
and that's what he
was talking about,

00:25:42.807 --> 00:25:45.410
that all of the policy people
said, you do it the other way,

00:25:45.410 --> 00:25:48.313
you do the Palestinians first
and then the rest will happen.

00:25:48.313 --> 00:25:50.115
But he said, no, we're
gonna try it this way.

00:25:50.115 --> 00:25:51.316
And it actually worked.

00:25:51.316 --> 00:25:53.552 align:start size:84% position:16%
But in essence, you're
saying these guys,

00:25:53.552 --> 00:25:55.453 align:start size:88% position:13%
they don't like
change, so I'm guessing

00:25:55.453 --> 00:25:56.955
you're getting pushback
from your own people

00:25:56.955 --> 00:25:59.090
as these things are happening.

00:25:59.090 --> 00:26:00.358
- Of course.

00:26:00.358 --> 00:26:01.626
And you can see that, by
the way, when we leave,

00:26:01.626 --> 00:26:04.496
they immediately begin
to fudge a little bit

00:26:04.496 --> 00:26:05.931
on where the embassy's gonna be,

00:26:05.931 --> 00:26:07.465 align:start size:84% position:16%
whether it's really
gonna be in Jerusalem,

00:26:07.465 --> 00:26:09.568
are we gonna have a consulate
there too for the Palestinian?

00:26:09.568 --> 00:26:13.471
So, you could see the machine
start to push back against it

00:26:13.471 --> 00:26:14.773
even after we leave.

00:26:14.773 --> 00:26:16.374
But we certainly suffered that.

00:26:17.576 --> 00:26:19.077
We were mocked, right?

00:26:19.077 --> 00:26:21.813 align:start size:97% position:3%
Jared's proposal was
called deal of the century,

00:26:21.813 --> 00:26:25.116
just dripping with sarcasm.

00:26:25.116 --> 00:26:27.586
But in the end, we
understood something

00:26:27.586 --> 00:26:29.521
I think that frankly,

00:26:29.521 --> 00:26:31.723
Republican and Democrat
administrations alike

00:26:31.723 --> 00:26:32.958
hadn't recognized.

00:26:32.958 --> 00:26:35.360
We came to believe
that these nations,

00:26:35.360 --> 00:26:37.896
the Gulf State Arab nations knew

00:26:37.896 --> 00:26:39.965
that the Palestinian
cause was important,

00:26:39.965 --> 00:26:42.000
but it wasn't their
highest priority.

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.536
That is, I want good
things for the people

00:26:44.536 --> 00:26:47.405 align:start size:97% position:3%
that live in Judea and
Samaria, whatever ethnicity,

00:26:47.405 --> 00:26:48.873
whatever religion they are,

00:26:48.873 --> 00:26:50.809
I want good things for
people in Saudi Arabia

00:26:50.809 --> 00:26:52.310
and the Emirates,
but in the end,

00:26:52.310 --> 00:26:53.979 align:start size:84% position:16%
we're gonna go
deliver good outcomes.

00:26:53.979 --> 00:26:57.749 align:start size:88% position:13%
And Abu Mazen the leader
of the Palestinians

00:26:57.749 --> 00:27:00.018 align:start size:84% position:16%
in Judea and Samaria,
he's a terrorist,

00:27:00.018 --> 00:27:01.987 align:start size:97% position:3%
and there was no chance that
guy was gonna cut a deal,

00:27:01.987 --> 00:27:03.888 align:start size:81% position:19%
so we didn't waste
any time trying

00:27:03.888 --> 00:27:06.858
to get a deal done, right,
to draw lines on the map.

00:27:06.858 --> 00:27:11.863 align:start size:97% position:3%
We threw that out in the
way that both Bush and Obama

00:27:13.064 --> 00:27:15.033
and all of them had
tried to negotiate.

00:27:15.033 --> 00:27:17.502
We knew there was a
solution that said,

00:27:17.502 --> 00:27:19.471
we're happy to work on
the Palestinian issue,

00:27:19.471 --> 00:27:21.573 align:start size:84% position:16%
happy to drive
towards a conclusion,

00:27:21.573 --> 00:27:23.642
but in the meantime we're
gonna go deliver peace

00:27:23.642 --> 00:27:25.477
in the region. And we did.

00:27:25.477 --> 00:27:28.079 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Do you think
either in that region

00:27:28.079 --> 00:27:30.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
or really all over the
world that other countries

00:27:30.415 --> 00:27:32.450
kind of miss that
American leadership

00:27:32.450 --> 00:27:33.685
that does seem to be lost?

00:27:33.685 --> 00:27:35.086
As I said, I just
did an hour show

00:27:35.086 --> 00:27:36.621
on the World Economic Forum.

00:27:36.621 --> 00:27:39.224
We seem to be outsourcing
all of our decision making

00:27:39.224 --> 00:27:41.726 align:start size:97% position:3%
to groups that have
nothing to do with our laws

00:27:41.726 --> 00:27:44.095
or our founding, or
anything like that.

00:27:44.095 --> 00:27:46.464 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I don't have to guess.
I know it to be true.

00:27:47.632 --> 00:27:48.900
I still stay in touch
with a handful of folks

00:27:48.900 --> 00:27:50.435 align:start size:84% position:16%
around the world
who call me and say,

00:27:50.435 --> 00:27:52.504
what the heck is going on?

00:27:52.504 --> 00:27:54.739
And it's not even just that.

00:27:54.739 --> 00:27:57.242
Dave, it's not even that
we agreed with him always.

00:27:57.242 --> 00:28:00.011
We had big knockdown, drag
out fights with friends,

00:28:00.011 --> 00:28:02.781
with allies, with
our adversaries.

00:28:02.781 --> 00:28:05.083 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you could, when I
was a secretary of state,

00:28:05.083 --> 00:28:06.451
you could get me on the phone,

00:28:06.451 --> 00:28:08.386 align:start size:84% position:16%
you could have a
serious conversation.

00:28:08.386 --> 00:28:10.455
I would tell you very much
what America was gonna do,

00:28:10.455 --> 00:28:11.690
how we were gonna behave.

00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:13.091 align:start size:88% position:13%
I would listen, I'd take
on board their ideas.

00:28:13.091 --> 00:28:14.826
If we could make
it work, we would.

00:28:14.826 --> 00:28:17.228
But you didn't have to guess,
you didn't have to wonder,

00:28:17.228 --> 00:28:21.032
I wasn't apologizing
for America every day.

00:28:21.032 --> 00:28:22.634
I was talking about
America as a force

00:28:22.634 --> 00:28:23.768
for good in the world.

00:28:23.768 --> 00:28:26.137 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I think that
leadership in the world

00:28:26.137 --> 00:28:27.572
is something that these nations,

00:28:27.572 --> 00:28:30.008 align:start size:97% position:3%
even those that aren't
particularly friendly to us,

00:28:30.008 --> 00:28:33.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think those nations miss
that true north anchor

00:28:33.078 --> 00:28:34.846
inside the United States.

00:28:34.846 --> 00:28:37.315 align:start position:0%
- Yeah, it's interesting because
our media seems to hate it

00:28:37.315 --> 00:28:39.284
more than the countries, right?

00:28:39.284 --> 00:28:40.585
The other countries
seem to want it.

00:28:40.585 --> 00:28:41.986
That's what you're saying.

00:28:41.986 --> 00:28:43.188
But it's our own media,

00:28:43.188 --> 00:28:45.290 align:start size:88% position:13%
which seems to actively
despise our ability

00:28:45.290 --> 00:28:47.025
to have influence.

00:28:47.025 --> 00:28:48.626
- You see this.

00:28:48.626 --> 00:28:51.730 align:start size:97% position:3%
You see this in every
element of American policy,

00:28:51.730 --> 00:28:54.699
not just in our national
security policy, right?

00:28:54.699 --> 00:28:56.334 align:start size:84% position:16%
In our schools,
they're teaching kids

00:28:56.334 --> 00:28:57.902
that America's a racist nation.

00:28:57.902 --> 00:29:00.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's an oppressor
class in our universities.

00:29:00.505 --> 00:29:03.641 align:start position:0%
They can't understand that
there's just two genders, right?

00:29:03.641 --> 00:29:08.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
These are ideas that undermine
the central propositions

00:29:08.146 --> 00:29:11.883
that have made America so
exceptional for 250 years.

00:29:11.883 --> 00:29:14.753
And whether it's in national
security or education at home

00:29:14.753 --> 00:29:19.657 align:start size:97% position:3%
or crime, always these
folks are working the edges.

00:29:19.657 --> 00:29:23.528
And I've had some folks say,
Mike, you have to compromise.

00:29:23.528 --> 00:29:26.364 align:start size:88% position:13%
You were a diplomat, you
have to give an inch.

00:29:26.364 --> 00:29:29.467
But the truth is there's
places you can compromise.

00:29:29.467 --> 00:29:31.870
If my son wanted to
go to bed at 8:30

00:29:31.870 --> 00:29:33.138
and I thought 8:00
was the right time,

00:29:33.138 --> 00:29:35.373
8:07 sounds good, right?

00:29:35.373 --> 00:29:39.244 align:start size:84% position:16%
But on things that
really matter, the
American value system,

00:29:39.244 --> 00:29:41.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
the central
understandings of family,

00:29:41.813 --> 00:29:46.050
the idea that this is in
fact the most noble nation

00:29:46.050 --> 00:29:48.820 align:start size:84% position:16%
to ever exist in the
history of civil.

00:29:48.820 --> 00:29:51.656 align:start size:88% position:13%
On those things, you
can't round the corners.

00:29:51.656 --> 00:29:52.590
You can't. You literally,

00:29:52.590 --> 00:29:53.892
because once you begin to say,

00:29:53.892 --> 00:29:55.960
well, it's a good
point, you're done.

00:29:55.960 --> 00:29:58.429 align:start size:97% position:3%
Because they will drive a
truck through the damn thing.

00:29:58.429 --> 00:30:00.865 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we just simply
can't let that happen.

00:30:00.865 --> 00:30:02.934
- So what do you think
is really going on here

00:30:02.934 --> 00:30:06.337 align:start size:97% position:3%
with this globalist
situation and these meetings

00:30:06.337 --> 00:30:09.841 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they have in Davos
and all these other places

00:30:09.841 --> 00:30:11.442
where a whole bunch of people,

00:30:11.442 --> 00:30:14.412 align:start size:97% position:3%
nobody seemingly to
represent the United States,

00:30:14.412 --> 00:30:17.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
nobody to represent
the individual.

00:30:17.081 --> 00:30:18.349
We send Americans there,

00:30:18.349 --> 00:30:20.318
but they very rarely
talk about America.

00:30:20.318 --> 00:30:21.820 align:start size:84% position:16%
Actually, on my
show the other day,

00:30:21.820 --> 00:30:24.889
we played a clip of 2018
when President Trump went

00:30:24.889 --> 00:30:26.391 align:start size:84% position:16%
and he started
talking about America.

00:30:26.391 --> 00:30:28.126 align:start size:84% position:16%
And they were not
very happy with him.

00:30:28.126 --> 00:30:32.130 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is the actual
influence of these groups?

00:30:32.130 --> 00:30:34.732
Like, is it as scary as it seems

00:30:34.732 --> 00:30:37.035 align:start size:84% position:16%
when we're watching
these clips on YouTube

00:30:37.035 --> 00:30:38.002
and everywhere else?

00:30:39.137 --> 00:30:40.805
- I actually think some of this

00:30:40.805 --> 00:30:45.243
is just a bunch of gasbags
meeting to have confabs.

00:30:45.243 --> 00:30:46.678
- I hope you're right.

00:30:46.678 --> 00:30:47.478
- Yeah.

00:30:48.847 --> 00:30:52.217 align:start size:97% position:3%
But look, there is a
globalist agenda out there,

00:30:52.217 --> 00:30:54.619 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's centered at
Turtle Bay in New York

00:30:54.619 --> 00:30:56.020
at the United Nations, right?

00:30:56.020 --> 00:30:58.122
That is the hub, that
is the focal point,

00:30:58.122 --> 00:31:01.526 align:start size:97% position:3%
that is the quasi-governmental
organization, the NGO

00:31:01.526 --> 00:31:03.895
that drives much
of this narrative.

00:31:03.895 --> 00:31:08.900
It then bleeds over into human
rights activism from the left

00:31:10.301 --> 00:31:13.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
and into American and
global businesses as well

00:31:13.238 --> 00:31:15.440
who don't stand up to
the political pressures

00:31:15.440 --> 00:31:16.674
that they need to.

00:31:16.674 --> 00:31:21.312 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I don't worry
as much about places

00:31:21.312 --> 00:31:23.114
that where these
folks go to gather,

00:31:23.114 --> 00:31:24.782 align:start size:97% position:3%
some of them are just there
doing commercial deals

00:31:24.782 --> 00:31:26.050 align:start size:81% position:19%
that'll end up
being really great

00:31:26.050 --> 00:31:28.019
to create tens of
thousands of jobs

00:31:28.019 --> 00:31:29.320 align:start size:81% position:19%
for the United
States of America.

00:31:29.320 --> 00:31:32.056 align:start size:88% position:13%
I worry about the
United States government

00:31:32.056 --> 00:31:34.292
and its unwillingness to accept

00:31:34.292 --> 00:31:36.327
that most of these institutions,

00:31:36.327 --> 00:31:40.732
the UN, the IAEA, I
could go on, the WTO,

00:31:40.732 --> 00:31:43.201
they have undermined
American sovereignty

00:31:43.201 --> 00:31:45.203
and we've allowed
that to happen.

00:31:45.203 --> 00:31:46.471
And the Chinese have figured out

00:31:46.471 --> 00:31:48.873
how to run many of
those institutions.

00:31:48.873 --> 00:31:51.976
Those are the places
that actually exert
influence and power

00:31:51.976 --> 00:31:55.280
and have the capacity to
shape both American thought

00:31:55.280 --> 00:31:57.815
and the way America
engages in the world.

00:31:57.815 --> 00:32:02.687 align:start position:0%
And you don't have to leave
the UN but you better make sure

00:32:02.687 --> 00:32:04.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
that you are not permitting
the United Nation

00:32:04.656 --> 00:32:06.157 align:start size:84% position:16%
to behave in ways that
undermine America.

00:32:06.157 --> 00:32:07.759 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we never allowed
that to happen.

00:32:07.759 --> 00:32:09.827 align:start size:97% position:3%
- They could at least pay
their parking tickets, right?

00:32:09.827 --> 00:32:11.362
Isn't that a huge
scandal every year?

00:32:11.362 --> 00:32:13.097 align:start size:84% position:16%
They don't pay their
parking tickets.

00:32:13.097 --> 00:32:15.199
- Yes, they should pay
their parking tickets

00:32:15.199 --> 00:32:18.102
and they should stick to
their knitting as well.

00:32:18.102 --> 00:32:20.104
- Were you surprised by
Trump's instincts on that

00:32:20.104 --> 00:32:22.206
as a guy who wasn't part
of the political class,

00:32:22.206 --> 00:32:24.175
that that really was like
one of his main things

00:32:24.175 --> 00:32:26.511 align:start size:97% position:3%
from beat one, you guys
are gonna pay what you owe.

00:32:26.511 --> 00:32:28.079
We're not gonna foot
the bill on all this.

00:32:28.079 --> 00:32:30.081
We're not just gonna give
you endless resources.

00:32:30.081 --> 00:32:32.884
That he just kind of got
that right right away.

00:32:32.884 --> 00:32:35.219
- Not surprised at all.
He campaigned on it.

00:32:35.219 --> 00:32:37.722
He intuitively understood it.

00:32:37.722 --> 00:32:39.190
Business guy, came
from the real world.

00:32:39.190 --> 00:32:41.659 align:start size:84% position:16%
What do you do? You
pay your bills, right?

00:32:41.659 --> 00:32:43.861
And if you don't,
bad things happen.

00:32:43.861 --> 00:32:45.129
Have to file bankruptcy, right?

00:32:45.129 --> 00:32:47.465
He'd lived all of
that in his life.

00:32:48.900 --> 00:32:53.037
No, he understood too that
these things aren't infinite,

00:32:53.037 --> 00:32:56.574
so we can survive in America
spending a whole bunch of money

00:32:56.574 --> 00:32:59.110
all across the world for
a while, but in the end,

00:32:59.110 --> 00:33:00.645 align:start size:81% position:19%
you gotta make
sure you take care

00:33:00.645 --> 00:33:02.513
of the things that matter
most to people back home.

00:33:02.513 --> 00:33:07.218
And he grasped that in a
way that so many did not.

00:33:07.218 --> 00:33:10.188 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I think America was better
off as a result of that.

00:33:10.188 --> 00:33:13.458
- So you were secretary
of state during COVID,

00:33:13.458 --> 00:33:16.661
and that kind of
changed the world.

00:33:16.661 --> 00:33:19.030
Can you talk about
that a little bit?

00:33:19.030 --> 00:33:21.399
- Yeah. So, a couple things.

00:33:21.399 --> 00:33:24.702 align:start size:97% position:3%
One, I ran a massive airline
for a bunch of months.

00:33:24.702 --> 00:33:27.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
We had Americans stranded
all over the world.

00:33:27.038 --> 00:33:29.340
We brought back a hundred
thousand plus Americans

00:33:29.340 --> 00:33:31.609
who'd had roadways,
buses, airplanes

00:33:31.609 --> 00:33:33.611
pulled out from under 'em,

00:33:33.611 --> 00:33:35.480 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so we went and tried
to round them all up,

00:33:35.480 --> 00:33:36.914
which was amazing work.

00:33:36.914 --> 00:33:39.617 align:start position:0%
That State Department, actually
I gave them full credit

00:33:39.617 --> 00:33:41.185
for having managed this process

00:33:41.185 --> 00:33:44.722 align:start size:97% position:3%
to help get these people
back home outta tough places.

00:33:44.722 --> 00:33:46.190
But more broadly,

00:33:46.190 --> 00:33:49.227 align:start size:97% position:3%
it gave us two opportunities
and a couple challenges.

00:33:49.227 --> 00:33:51.963
First challenge was, look,
this virus almost certainly

00:33:51.963 --> 00:33:53.031
came from the Chinese lab.

00:33:53.031 --> 00:33:54.298
And we were immediately,

00:33:54.298 --> 00:33:58.002
I think I said this on a
TV show in March of '20,

00:33:59.237 --> 00:34:02.907
maybe it was April and,
just pillaring for hate,

00:34:02.907 --> 00:34:06.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was a racist and
the anti-China racist.

00:34:06.611 --> 00:34:10.081
Nope, it came from the
lab almost certainly.

00:34:10.081 --> 00:34:12.650 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Also China, Chinese
is not a race,

00:34:12.650 --> 00:34:14.185 align:start size:84% position:16%
but that's a different
thing, but okay.

00:34:14.185 --> 00:34:16.888 align:start size:84% position:16%
- No. It's all crazy.
- Yeah.

00:34:18.623 --> 00:34:20.792
- But even more important
than where it came from,

00:34:20.792 --> 00:34:22.126
the Chinese leadership knew

00:34:22.126 --> 00:34:24.195 align:start size:81% position:19%
that they had a
pretty contagious,

00:34:24.195 --> 00:34:28.099 align:start size:97% position:3%
relatively lethal virus on
their hands by the fall of '19

00:34:28.099 --> 00:34:31.335 align:start position:0%
and decided to put tens of
thousands of people on airplanes

00:34:31.335 --> 00:34:32.470
and murder.

00:34:32.470 --> 00:34:34.872 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I say that
intentionally, murder

00:34:34.872 --> 00:34:36.307
hundreds of thousands of people

00:34:36.307 --> 00:34:37.875
all across this country.

00:34:37.875 --> 00:34:39.110
They had a choice to make.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:40.812
The choice they made
was load airplanes

00:34:40.812 --> 00:34:42.180
send them to Milan, Italy.

00:34:43.581 --> 00:34:45.817
The Chinese Communist Party
must be held accountable

00:34:45.817 --> 00:34:47.251
for this.

00:34:47.251 --> 00:34:49.253 align:start size:97% position:3%
Look, they don't care
about human life, so be it.

00:34:49.253 --> 00:34:51.956
But when you transmit that
to the rest of the world

00:34:51.956 --> 00:34:53.391
and you kill people
all around the world,

00:34:53.391 --> 00:34:55.593
there's a place for
real accountability.

00:34:56.761 --> 00:34:59.130 align:start size:88% position:13%
The good news is I think
Americans came to see

00:34:59.130 --> 00:35:01.499 align:start size:97% position:3%
how bad the Chinese
Communist Party really was.

00:35:01.499 --> 00:35:02.733
The risk to America,

00:35:02.733 --> 00:35:04.936
if we outsourced all
of our manufacturing,

00:35:06.337 --> 00:35:09.373 align:start size:97% position:3%
certainly semiconductors
and national security stuff,

00:35:09.373 --> 00:35:12.944 align:start size:97% position:3%
but think basic things like
simple pharmaceuticals,

00:35:12.944 --> 00:35:17.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
the capacity for our
medical system to operate

00:35:17.415 --> 00:35:19.183
without Chinese supply chains.

00:35:19.183 --> 00:35:21.486
I think American people can
see that that was a bad idea

00:35:21.486 --> 00:35:25.289 align:start position:0%
and those businesses are
starting to come back to America

00:35:25.289 --> 00:35:27.458 align:start position:0%
and to places that we can count
on to partners and friends.

00:35:27.458 --> 00:35:29.327
And that is a good thing.

00:35:29.327 --> 00:35:31.896
The last thing was,
COVID had the upshot

00:35:31.896 --> 00:35:35.266
of giving parents a
crack and a window

00:35:35.266 --> 00:35:37.969
into what their kids were
being taught in schools.

00:35:37.969 --> 00:35:41.506
And ain't no mama wants
their kid to be taught

00:35:41.506 --> 00:35:44.075 align:start size:88% position:13%
that America is a racist
nation and that math

00:35:44.075 --> 00:35:46.110 align:start size:84% position:16%
and science and
reading don't matter.

00:35:46.110 --> 00:35:49.547 align:start position:0%
And I think we've seen a
fundamental transformation about

00:35:49.547 --> 00:35:52.049 align:start size:88% position:13%
how parents think
about public education.

00:35:52.049 --> 00:35:54.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
They wanna make sure
their kids get a fair shot

00:35:54.018 --> 00:35:55.753
at the American opportunity.

00:35:55.753 --> 00:35:58.055
And I was all across
the country last year

00:35:58.055 --> 00:35:59.690
campaigning for candidates.

00:35:59.690 --> 00:36:01.526
It didn't go as well
as I would've hoped,

00:36:01.526 --> 00:36:04.228 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I was out there grinding
away listening to folks,

00:36:04.228 --> 00:36:06.264
and they are serious about this.

00:36:06.264 --> 00:36:10.034
And the fact that we were
all watching more closely

00:36:10.034 --> 00:36:11.702
what our kids were up to,

00:36:11.702 --> 00:36:13.638
I think is a net good
thing for America.

00:36:13.638 --> 00:36:15.239
- Yeah. And by the way,
it's happening right now.

00:36:15.239 --> 00:36:17.975 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, Kim Reynolds is
doing school choice in Iowa.

00:36:17.975 --> 00:36:19.710
Huckabee is gonna be
doing it in Arkansas.

00:36:19.710 --> 00:36:22.580
Clearly something good's
happening here in Florida.

00:36:22.580 --> 00:36:25.983 align:start size:97% position:3%
But on the first part of
that, when you guys realized

00:36:25.983 --> 00:36:28.486 align:start size:84% position:16%
that in essence it
was coming from China,

00:36:28.486 --> 00:36:30.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
either fully,
intentionally or not,

00:36:30.121 --> 00:36:31.422 align:start size:84% position:16%
or then they were
sending these planes

00:36:31.422 --> 00:36:33.257
first to Italy and
then everywhere.

00:36:33.257 --> 00:36:34.759
I'm guessing you
got on the phone

00:36:34.759 --> 00:36:36.327 align:start size:84% position:16%
with some sort of
Chinese counterpart.

00:36:36.327 --> 00:36:39.330 align:start size:97% position:3%
I mean, did they just
stonewall you on everything?

00:36:39.330 --> 00:36:40.765
Did they admit anything?

00:36:40.765 --> 00:36:44.902 align:start size:97% position:3%
Was there any level of
accountability or anything?

00:36:44.902 --> 00:36:46.204
- Total stonewall.

00:36:46.204 --> 00:36:48.606 align:start size:88% position:13%
I tell this story, it's
an important story.

00:36:48.606 --> 00:36:53.611 align:start size:88% position:13%
As we rounded from 2019
into 2020, the CDC,

00:36:56.047 --> 00:36:57.748 align:start size:84% position:16%
they all had
counterparts in China.

00:36:57.748 --> 00:37:00.251 align:start size:97% position:3%
And they'd been talking
because there was this rumor

00:37:00.251 --> 00:37:01.786
about what was going on there.

00:37:01.786 --> 00:37:03.588
And right at the
first of the year,

00:37:03.588 --> 00:37:05.756
total shutdown, locked out.

00:37:05.756 --> 00:37:10.294
I was asked by Mr. Redfield to
call my Chinese counterpart,

00:37:10.294 --> 00:37:11.829 align:start size:88% position:13%
the foreign minister
and the state councilor.

00:37:11.829 --> 00:37:14.665
I did. Nothing, not a word.

00:37:14.665 --> 00:37:16.867 align:start size:94% position:6%
The World Health
Organization gets shut out

00:37:16.867 --> 00:37:18.402
when they tried to investigate.

00:37:18.402 --> 00:37:20.671
Sadly, they just bent a knee
and said, Nope, everything,

00:37:20.671 --> 00:37:22.406
nothing to see here, folks,

00:37:22.406 --> 00:37:24.942
so the WHO failed
the world as well.

00:37:24.942 --> 00:37:27.979 align:start size:97% position:3%
But yeah, they went into
complete information lockdown,

00:37:29.413 --> 00:37:31.716
hiding from the world what
they most certainly knew

00:37:31.716 --> 00:37:33.117
about what had happened there.

00:37:33.117 --> 00:37:35.853 align:start size:97% position:3%
- How do you as the
secretary of state coordinate

00:37:35.853 --> 00:37:39.957
or work with those, the
WHO, the NIH, the CDC,

00:37:39.957 --> 00:37:41.192
all of these things.

00:37:41.192 --> 00:37:42.293
I mean, you're dealing
with borders and planes,

00:37:42.293 --> 00:37:43.227
and all of that stuff.

00:37:43.227 --> 00:37:44.695
Are you directly telling,

00:37:44.695 --> 00:37:46.897
are they basically telling
you you've gotta shut borders

00:37:46.897 --> 00:37:48.366
and you can't do this,
and you gotta do that?

00:37:48.366 --> 00:37:50.768
Like, who's actually in
charge at that point?

00:37:50.768 --> 00:37:53.237 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah, so the senior
decisions about

00:37:53.237 --> 00:37:54.739 align:start size:84% position:16%
what America was gonna
do in the response

00:37:54.739 --> 00:37:56.674 align:start size:84% position:16%
were made by President
Trump himself,

00:37:56.674 --> 00:38:00.745
with the advice from me and
from Department of Defense,

00:38:00.745 --> 00:38:03.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
from NIH, CDC, all of
his advisors were around,

00:38:03.848 --> 00:38:06.584
the vice president led
the response task force.

00:38:06.584 --> 00:38:08.319
But in the end, the
big decisions about

00:38:08.319 --> 00:38:09.487
whether to close
our borders or not

00:38:09.487 --> 00:38:11.055
were made by the president.

00:38:11.055 --> 00:38:12.923
- Do you guys think
you botched anything?

00:38:12.923 --> 00:38:14.325 align:start size:81% position:19%
I mean, if you
were to look back,

00:38:14.325 --> 00:38:15.860 align:start position:0%
would you have done this
differently or that differently

00:38:15.860 --> 00:38:18.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
or advised him
differently, or anything?

00:38:18.362 --> 00:38:19.830
- I thought about this a lot.

00:38:20.865 --> 00:38:23.668 align:start size:84% position:16%
In perfect hindsight,
you can say

00:38:23.668 --> 00:38:25.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there was
information we didn't know

00:38:25.102 --> 00:38:26.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
or we weren't thinking
about quite right.

00:38:26.871 --> 00:38:28.572
I think we got good pieces

00:38:28.572 --> 00:38:31.042 align:start size:84% position:16%
of the actual physical
response right.

00:38:31.042 --> 00:38:33.878
But I think we got some
of the messaging wrong.

00:38:33.878 --> 00:38:35.546
And then as time moved on

00:38:35.546 --> 00:38:37.048 align:start size:84% position:16%
and more information
was available,

00:38:37.048 --> 00:38:41.786
I think Dr. Fauci did terrible
things by talking about this

00:38:41.786 --> 00:38:44.021
in a way that kept
our schools closed

00:38:44.021 --> 00:38:45.256
for as long as they did.

00:38:45.256 --> 00:38:47.692
We knew that the
kids were unlikely

00:38:47.692 --> 00:38:51.228
to have serious large scale
ramifications from this.

00:38:52.363 --> 00:38:54.832
We told teachers, Oh,
you can stay home.

00:38:54.832 --> 00:38:56.701 align:start size:88% position:13%
When we told nurses
they had to go to work.

00:38:56.701 --> 00:38:58.169
They're all important,

00:38:58.169 --> 00:39:01.672 align:start size:97% position:3%
but why on earth we didn't
open our schools more quickly?

00:39:01.672 --> 00:39:04.141 align:start size:97% position:3%
Why we were so closing
that up and we had churches

00:39:04.141 --> 00:39:08.479
and synagogues shut down too
is incomprehensible to me.

00:39:08.479 --> 00:39:09.647
- Do you think it's fair to say

00:39:09.647 --> 00:39:11.182 align:start size:84% position:16%
that China did
this intentionally?

00:39:11.182 --> 00:39:14.085
Maybe not the leak itself,
but that the export of it,

00:39:14.085 --> 00:39:16.087 align:start size:84% position:16%
and when you're being
stonewalled in all
of these things.

00:39:16.087 --> 00:39:20.358 align:start size:97% position:3%
That this was sort of the plan
to get western democracies

00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:22.226
to, in essence turn
against their people,

00:39:22.226 --> 00:39:25.296
become a little bit more like
China rather than China become

00:39:25.296 --> 00:39:26.731
a little bit more like us,

00:39:26.731 --> 00:39:28.866 align:start position:0%
which is what I think most
people thought was gonna happen,

00:39:28.866 --> 00:39:31.135
for the last 30 years,
something like that.

00:39:31.135 --> 00:39:32.536
- Dave, you got
it exactly right.

00:39:32.536 --> 00:39:34.004
Yes. Absolutely intentional.

00:39:34.004 --> 00:39:37.375 align:start size:97% position:3%
At the very least we can argue
knowing versus intentional

00:39:37.375 --> 00:39:40.945
as absolutely knowingly sent
this virus around the world.

00:39:40.945 --> 00:39:43.614
And from my perspective, the
difference between knowing

00:39:43.614 --> 00:39:45.282
and intent is zero in this case.

00:39:45.282 --> 00:39:48.018
They intended this virus
to go around and they knew

00:39:48.018 --> 00:39:50.388 align:start size:88% position:13%
it was gonna kill people
all across the globe.

00:39:51.589 --> 00:39:53.557
What were their
motives for that?

00:39:53.557 --> 00:39:56.394
We can all argue about.
I don't know the answer.

00:39:56.394 --> 00:39:58.162
But here's what
we know for sure.

00:39:58.162 --> 00:40:01.098
A decent nation, a nation
that cared about humanity,

00:40:01.098 --> 00:40:02.266
would've opened the doors,

00:40:02.266 --> 00:40:03.768 align:start size:84% position:16%
brought in the world's
leading experts,

00:40:03.768 --> 00:40:05.269
wouldn't have let
anybody travel,

00:40:05.269 --> 00:40:07.338
would've locked down that
virus as best they could

00:40:07.338 --> 00:40:10.174
where they found it
and have given them

00:40:10.174 --> 00:40:13.110
the global community, and
frankly, it's America,

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:15.045
mostly America's best
scientist the capacity

00:40:15.045 --> 00:40:16.714
to understand what
was going on there,

00:40:16.714 --> 00:40:19.350 align:start size:84% position:16%
so that you can
develop solutions that
actually make sense.

00:40:19.350 --> 00:40:21.051
Not just for China, but
for the entire world.

00:40:21.051 --> 00:40:23.854
And they chose exactly
the opposite course.

00:40:23.854 --> 00:40:25.189
- So, what do we do about that?

00:40:25.189 --> 00:40:28.526 align:start size:84% position:16%
I mean, if that
actually is the case,

00:40:28.526 --> 00:40:30.828
let's say you were to have
another job in your future,

00:40:30.828 --> 00:40:35.032
perhaps, what do you do
if that really is true?

00:40:36.834 --> 00:40:38.469
- It's real.

00:40:38.469 --> 00:40:40.571 align:start size:97% position:3%
Don't kid yourself about the
World Health Organization

00:40:40.571 --> 00:40:42.106
saving the lives of Americans.

00:40:42.106 --> 00:40:44.642
They're not going to, you have
to take this upon ourselves.

00:40:44.642 --> 00:40:46.911
We're happy to work with
folks around the world.

00:40:46.911 --> 00:40:49.980
These kinds of things
are global problems,

00:40:49.980 --> 00:40:51.482 align:start size:84% position:16%
but America's
gonna have to lead.

00:40:51.482 --> 00:40:53.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we can't do it by
providing a bunch of money

00:40:53.651 --> 00:40:55.386
to guys at the World
Health Organization

00:40:55.386 --> 00:40:56.921
that don't really give a darn

00:40:56.921 --> 00:40:59.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the second and
third order ramifications

00:40:59.690 --> 00:41:01.592
of their failures.

00:41:01.592 --> 00:41:03.093
More broadly for China,

00:41:03.093 --> 00:41:05.696
we could talk about this
for an awfully long time.

00:41:07.198 --> 00:41:10.534
Republicans and Democrats
alike permitted themselves

00:41:10.534 --> 00:41:12.770
the fantasy that
you just described.

00:41:12.770 --> 00:41:15.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
We thought they'd
become more like us,

00:41:15.139 --> 00:41:17.241
and we've known for
at least a decade,

00:41:17.241 --> 00:41:19.043
maybe two, that wasn't true.

00:41:19.043 --> 00:41:20.377
And we just let it keep going,

00:41:20.377 --> 00:41:22.279
and we let 'em walk all over us.

00:41:22.279 --> 00:41:24.548 align:start size:84% position:16%
The Chinese built
their massive economy

00:41:24.548 --> 00:41:26.650
on the backs of the
American worker,

00:41:26.650 --> 00:41:28.586
and we don't need
to let that happen,

00:41:28.586 --> 00:41:31.522
and so I gave a speech
in the spring of '20

00:41:31.522 --> 00:41:33.357
that basically said
China's an adversary,

00:41:33.357 --> 00:41:35.226
much like the Soviet Union.

00:41:35.226 --> 00:41:37.461
Ronald Reagan said,
we win, they lose.

00:41:37.461 --> 00:41:39.163
That's what's gonna have
to happen here as well.

00:41:39.163 --> 00:41:41.765
We're gonna have to win and
they're gonna have to lose.

00:41:41.765 --> 00:41:43.868
We have the capacity to do that.

00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:47.304 align:start size:97% position:3%
We should make sure that
China is treated reciprocally.

00:41:47.304 --> 00:41:49.607
That is, what's a good example.

00:41:49.607 --> 00:41:51.976
The Chinese are trying
to build and buy land

00:41:51.976 --> 00:41:54.378 align:start size:84% position:16%
near American
military facilities.

00:41:54.378 --> 00:41:56.180
Dave, I'd ask everybody in
your audience, head out,

00:41:56.180 --> 00:41:57.715
call your real estate agent,

00:41:57.715 --> 00:42:00.150
try to buy land in China near
a Chinese military facility.

00:42:00.150 --> 00:42:02.319 align:start size:75% position:25%
Godspeed.
(Dave laughing)

00:42:02.319 --> 00:42:04.455
We should not let them-

00:42:04.455 --> 00:42:07.091
- They're not giving you
no money down on those.

00:42:07.091 --> 00:42:08.826 align:start size:94% position:6%
- My guess is your
realtor's gonna come back

00:42:08.826 --> 00:42:12.196 align:start size:97% position:3%
and say that's just a little
pricey. Can't get there.

00:42:12.196 --> 00:42:15.799
We should not let them use
our open society against us

00:42:15.799 --> 00:42:18.035
in the ways that we have.

00:42:18.035 --> 00:42:19.236
And American business,

00:42:19.236 --> 00:42:20.738 align:start size:84% position:16%
America's largest
financial institutions

00:42:20.738 --> 00:42:22.773
are all gonna have to come
on board, come on sides.

00:42:22.773 --> 00:42:27.444
If we need government power to
coax them in that direction,

00:42:27.444 --> 00:42:28.646
we've gotta do that.

00:42:28.646 --> 00:42:30.180 align:start size:81% position:19%
We've gotta return
to making sure

00:42:30.180 --> 00:42:33.117 align:start size:97% position:3%
we take care of working
class Americans here at home.

00:42:33.117 --> 00:42:37.521
And when we do, we will take
advantage of all the challenges

00:42:37.521 --> 00:42:38.789
that the Chinese have.

00:42:38.789 --> 00:42:40.824
They've got issues with
their aging population,

00:42:40.824 --> 00:42:42.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
they've got
financial challenges.

00:42:42.493 --> 00:42:44.361
They are not 10 feet tall.

00:42:44.361 --> 00:42:45.629
But when you lay down for them,

00:42:45.629 --> 00:42:47.231 align:start size:84% position:16%
they look like
they're 10 feet tall.

00:42:47.231 --> 00:42:49.600 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so, we just simply need
to stand up, push back,

00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:52.336
demand a world that
looks more like ours,

00:42:52.336 --> 00:42:54.238
a word with Western values.

00:42:54.238 --> 00:42:56.774
It means we gotta get it
right here at home too.

00:42:56.774 --> 00:42:58.075
If we do those things,

00:42:58.075 --> 00:43:00.411
then the Chinese dream
of an American decline

00:43:00.411 --> 00:43:03.213 align:start size:97% position:3%
will prove to be just that,
a fantasy and a dream.

00:43:03.213 --> 00:43:05.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Let me ask you about the
other big global event.

00:43:05.249 --> 00:43:09.086
Obviously Russia, Ukraine,
for the term that Trump had,

00:43:09.086 --> 00:43:11.488
and while you were secretary
of state, it was pretty quiet.

00:43:11.488 --> 00:43:13.991
Under Obama, Russia
takes back Crimea,

00:43:13.991 --> 00:43:16.226 align:start size:84% position:16%
but then it's quiet
under you guys.

00:43:16.226 --> 00:43:18.128
Now, obviously not so quiet.

00:43:18.128 --> 00:43:20.497
What would you be
doing right now?

00:43:20.497 --> 00:43:23.233 align:start size:84% position:16%
What would you be
advising Joe Biden on?

00:43:23.233 --> 00:43:25.569
And how do you feel about
this endless blank check

00:43:25.569 --> 00:43:28.372 align:start size:88% position:13%
that everybody
basically on both sides,

00:43:28.372 --> 00:43:30.874
except for pretty much, I think
Rand Paul and maybe Ted Cruz

00:43:30.874 --> 00:43:33.377
and a couple other guys
keep signing off on.

00:43:35.045 --> 00:43:38.148 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Goodness. I've been
asked this an awful lot.

00:43:38.148 --> 00:43:40.951
It was quiet on our watch
and you have to believe

00:43:40.951 --> 00:43:44.655 align:start size:97% position:3%
in a lot of coincidences to
think that we were just lucky.

00:43:44.655 --> 00:43:47.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
The truth is, I think
Vladimir Putin understood

00:43:47.391 --> 00:43:49.627
that we were different cast
of characters, all right?

00:43:49.627 --> 00:43:51.562
When the Iranians were
moving about the cabinet,

00:43:51.562 --> 00:43:53.797
we went and took out
Qasem Soleimani, right?

00:43:53.797 --> 00:43:57.001
Demonstrating that we were
gonna, in a very nuanced way,

00:43:57.001 --> 00:43:58.535
we didn't send 80,000 soldiers.

00:43:58.535 --> 00:44:00.738
We didn't go invade any place.

00:44:00.738 --> 00:44:03.907
We just sent a message
with absolute clarity

00:44:03.907 --> 00:44:05.676
that we were serious and real.

00:44:05.676 --> 00:44:08.679
- Was that your, the mother
of all bombs, was that you?

00:44:09.747 --> 00:44:11.949 align:start size:88% position:13%
- The strike on
Soleimani was something

00:44:11.949 --> 00:44:14.652 align:start size:97% position:3%
that I certainly recommended
to the president.

00:44:14.652 --> 00:44:17.888
And I write about this
because it was important

00:44:17.888 --> 00:44:21.959
not just to deter Iran, but
Chairman Kim in North Korea,

00:44:21.959 --> 00:44:26.430
who I spent way too much time
with, the Taliban, Xi Jinping,

00:44:26.430 --> 00:44:27.965
they all say, oh my goodness,

00:44:27.965 --> 00:44:29.233
these guys are serious, Pompeo.

00:44:29.233 --> 00:44:30.701
These guys are gonna,

00:44:30.701 --> 00:44:32.136
if they say they're
gonna do something,

00:44:32.136 --> 00:44:34.638
they actually are
going to do it.

00:44:34.638 --> 00:44:36.473
And Putin saw that
Biden wasn't that,

00:44:36.473 --> 00:44:40.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so you lose the bubble
and he invades Europe.

00:44:40.310 --> 00:44:43.847
As for what to do today,
every day this goes on,

00:44:43.847 --> 00:44:47.418
creates enormous risk
for us, for America.

00:44:47.418 --> 00:44:49.887
The risk that he uses a
tactical nuclear weapon,

00:44:49.887 --> 00:44:51.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
the risk that he
conducts a cyber campaign

00:44:51.922 --> 00:44:54.692
here in the States to
send a message to us.

00:44:54.692 --> 00:44:56.727
We gotta get this to end.

00:44:56.727 --> 00:44:59.029
I only know one way
to get it to end.

00:44:59.029 --> 00:45:00.998 align:start size:84% position:16%
And that is to
provide the Ukrainians

00:45:00.998 --> 00:45:02.766
with the tools that they need.

00:45:02.766 --> 00:45:05.703 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not for blank
checks, but I am for,

00:45:05.703 --> 00:45:08.238
if they're prepared to
defend their sovereignty

00:45:08.238 --> 00:45:10.974
and risk their own
boys and girls lives,

00:45:10.974 --> 00:45:12.910
I'm prepared to
help them do that

00:45:12.910 --> 00:45:15.779 align:start position:0%
against an authoritarian regime
that's killing civilians.

00:45:17.114 --> 00:45:20.317 align:start size:97% position:3%
We should then find a solution
that has two features.

00:45:20.317 --> 00:45:21.919 align:start size:84% position:16%
One, it's gonna have
to be acceptable

00:45:21.919 --> 00:45:24.188
to both the Russian people
and the Ukrainian people.

00:45:24.188 --> 00:45:26.890
Everybody talks about
Zelenskyy and Putin.

00:45:26.890 --> 00:45:28.425
It's just, there's
a lot going on here,

00:45:28.425 --> 00:45:30.094 align:start size:84% position:16%
and so you're gonna
have to find something

00:45:30.094 --> 00:45:33.063
that everybody can say, all
right, that is good enough.

00:45:33.063 --> 00:45:35.766 align:start size:88% position:13%
No one's gonna get
their maximalist dream.

00:45:35.766 --> 00:45:39.603 align:start position:0%
Second, we need to find a
solution that has a permanency.

00:45:39.603 --> 00:45:42.940 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I live in the real world,
nothing's ever permanent,

00:45:42.940 --> 00:45:45.409
but think 10, 20, 50
years of permanency.

00:45:45.409 --> 00:45:47.611
So that six months or
two years from now,

00:45:48.879 --> 00:45:50.114
Putin's not back at this,

00:45:50.114 --> 00:45:52.149 align:start size:84% position:16%
or his successor's not
back at this again.

00:45:52.149 --> 00:45:55.352
We have the capacity
to use American power,

00:45:55.352 --> 00:45:57.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
not our soldier, sailors,
airmen and marines,

00:45:57.821 --> 00:46:01.859 align:start position:0%
but American power to
facilitate a hastier conclusion

00:46:01.859 --> 00:46:05.295 align:start size:88% position:13%
to this and a relatively
permanent conclusion.

00:46:05.295 --> 00:46:07.765 align:start position:0%
That should be the American
mission for the American people.

00:46:07.765 --> 00:46:11.034 align:start position:0%
- Is the inherent problem there,
I think sort of two things.

00:46:11.034 --> 00:46:14.371
One that, I mean, Putin's
got nukes as you just said.

00:46:14.371 --> 00:46:18.542 align:start size:97% position:3%
And to make the guy with nukes
surrender is kind of tough

00:46:18.542 --> 00:46:20.477 align:start size:97% position:3%
'cause he's got the
ultimate weapon, number one.

00:46:20.477 --> 00:46:23.647 align:start size:97% position:3%
And number two, that if he
doesn't get a win out of this,

00:46:23.647 --> 00:46:24.882
if he doesn't get that off ramp,

00:46:24.882 --> 00:46:26.383
he doesn't want to
end up like Gaddafi

00:46:26.383 --> 00:46:29.787
and basically get stabbed
by one of his own people

00:46:29.787 --> 00:46:32.089
on the run for the last
couple weeks of his life.

00:46:32.089 --> 00:46:33.323
- Yeah, Dave, it's complicated.

00:46:33.323 --> 00:46:35.926
It's complicated for
both leaders, I think.

00:46:35.926 --> 00:46:37.961
Each of them have
constituencies.

00:46:37.961 --> 00:46:39.329
And it's different,
it's not a democracy.

00:46:39.329 --> 00:46:41.098
Nobody's gonna go
hold an election.

00:46:42.499 --> 00:46:47.304 align:start position:0%
But they both have to find ways
that they can move forward.

00:46:48.172 --> 00:46:49.807
I suspect that when this ends,

00:46:49.807 --> 00:46:54.311 align:start size:84% position:16%
each of those leaders
will struggle to
maintain their power.

00:46:54.311 --> 00:46:55.846
The Ukrainians are gonna
all look around and say,

00:46:55.846 --> 00:46:57.447 align:start size:81% position:19%
look what happened
to our country.

00:46:57.447 --> 00:46:58.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the Russians are
gonna look around and say,

00:46:58.682 --> 00:47:00.184 align:start size:81% position:19%
look what happened
to our country.

00:47:00.184 --> 00:47:03.220
And so, what I think
we should focus on

00:47:03.220 --> 00:47:06.190 align:start size:84% position:16%
is not the individuals
but the systems.

00:47:06.190 --> 00:47:08.959
Look, Ukraine, there was a
lot of corruption in Ukraine.

00:47:08.959 --> 00:47:11.028
The whole time I was
a secretary of state,

00:47:11.028 --> 00:47:15.766
we should never blink and
pretend that is not so,

00:47:15.766 --> 00:47:18.368 align:start size:84% position:16%
but we should strive
to take a country

00:47:18.368 --> 00:47:20.070 align:start size:84% position:16%
that has demonstrated
its willingness

00:47:20.070 --> 00:47:22.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
to be an American partner
and try to provide it

00:47:22.706 --> 00:47:24.541 align:start size:88% position:13%
with the tools to
protect its sovereignty.

00:47:24.541 --> 00:47:26.076
And if we get that right,

00:47:26.076 --> 00:47:28.212
we can find a space where
the Russian people can say,

00:47:28.212 --> 00:47:30.881 align:start size:88% position:13%
yep, this is quote, good
enough, end of quote.

00:47:30.881 --> 00:47:32.249
I'm convinced there is.

00:47:33.450 --> 00:47:35.052
Very few conflicts
like this one end

00:47:35.052 --> 00:47:38.856 align:start size:84% position:16%
with one side totally
annihilating and
defeating the other.

00:47:38.856 --> 00:47:41.825 align:start size:97% position:3%
The handful of cases, maybe
the American Civil War.

00:47:41.825 --> 00:47:44.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
We might, someone might
gimme two or three others,

00:47:44.895 --> 00:47:46.730
but, boy, there's very few.

00:47:46.730 --> 00:47:49.066
They always end up with
some level of compromise.

00:47:49.066 --> 00:47:51.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm confident this one
will end that way as well.

00:47:51.735 --> 00:47:53.403
And the sooner that happens,

00:47:53.403 --> 00:47:55.305
the less destruction in
Ukraine and the less,

00:47:55.305 --> 00:47:58.575
most importantly the less risk
to the United States as well.

00:47:58.575 --> 00:48:00.244
- I got one more
question for you.

00:48:00.244 --> 00:48:02.012
And you know what it is already,

00:48:02.012 --> 00:48:04.047
so I don't even have to ask you.

00:48:05.415 --> 00:48:08.185 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm not gonna tell you
about what's in the UFO files.

00:48:08.185 --> 00:48:10.020
Come on. (chuckles)

00:48:10.020 --> 00:48:11.255
- Exactly.

00:48:11.255 --> 00:48:12.522 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's actually what
I wanted to know.

00:48:12.522 --> 00:48:14.358
We can do that one off
camera, but of course.

00:48:14.358 --> 00:48:16.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, you wrote this
book, you're on the stump,

00:48:16.927 --> 00:48:18.695
people are mentioning your name.

00:48:18.695 --> 00:48:21.331 align:start size:97% position:3%
Your former boss has already
announced he's running.

00:48:21.331 --> 00:48:23.166
We're almost at the
season where people

00:48:23.166 --> 00:48:25.535
are getting in on this thing.

00:48:25.535 --> 00:48:27.871 align:start size:84% position:16%
There you go. I'm
giving you a softball.

00:48:27.871 --> 00:48:30.173
- We're getting close to
the time, you're right.

00:48:30.173 --> 00:48:33.377
Where it's time for those who
want to put themselves forward

00:48:33.377 --> 00:48:35.846
to make the case to the
American people to do so.

00:48:35.846 --> 00:48:38.882
Susan and I haven't made
that big decision just yet.

00:48:38.882 --> 00:48:41.018
We're working our way
to try and figure out

00:48:41.018 --> 00:48:42.920 align:start size:84% position:16%
if this is the right
time to do that,

00:48:42.920 --> 00:48:44.988
if we should go make that case.

00:48:44.988 --> 00:48:47.491
But I believe deeply in America.

00:48:47.491 --> 00:48:51.228 align:start size:84% position:16%
I grew up in a family
that understood

00:48:51.228 --> 00:48:53.697
the basic decency
of our country.

00:48:53.697 --> 00:48:56.099
That fight is something
I intend to stay in.

00:48:56.099 --> 00:48:59.169 align:start size:88% position:13%
Whether I end up
seeking political
office again in my life

00:48:59.169 --> 00:49:00.304
is yet to be determined.

00:49:00.304 --> 00:49:01.872
Only the good Lord knows.

00:49:01.872 --> 00:49:03.640 align:start size:97% position:3%
- All right, now gimme a
little something on the UFOs

00:49:03.640 --> 00:49:05.309
and then you're free.

00:49:05.309 --> 00:49:06.543
(Secretary Pompeo laughing)

00:49:06.543 --> 00:49:07.344
- Here's what I'd
say about the UFOs,

00:49:07.344 --> 00:49:08.812
we got bigger problems.

00:49:08.812 --> 00:49:11.481
(Dave laughing)

00:49:12.616 --> 00:49:14.318
- Secretary Pompeo,
I appreciate it,

00:49:14.318 --> 00:49:17.788
and if anything is to be
announced in the future,

00:49:17.788 --> 00:49:19.489
maybe we'll do this again.

00:49:19.489 --> 00:49:20.424
- Bless you, Dave.

00:49:20.424 --> 00:49:21.158
Thank you. Have a good day.

00:49:21.158 --> 00:49:22.693
- Thanks a lot.

00:49:22.693 --> 00:49:23.994
If you're looking
for more honest

00:49:23.994 --> 00:49:25.028 align:start size:97% position:3%
